existing-tool-capability investigation (so SKILL.md wires correctly to real 
commands across atlassian/bitbucket/slack/switcheroo/compass/twg + the three 
new tools) plus domain workflow/framework research for each of the nine 
skills. Subtask 2 needs only the SURFACE of the new tools — which is already 
enumerated in the parent description — so it does not block on Subtask 1's 
deep API investigation. Aggregator then materializes tool.json + 
implementations from Subtask 1 and the nine SKILL.md files from Subtask 2, 
cross-validating that every skill invocation maps to an actual tool command.",
  "coverage_complete": true,
  "gaps": "None within the 2-subtask constraint. Canonical source locations 
(SPIKE doc, Circuit Breaker Runbook, End-to-End ML Framework, role-doc §4) are
referenced but not pre-verified; workers must use agentic-search/rovo_search 
to locate them.",
  "aggregation_guidance": "The aggregator must (1) materialize three tool.json
definitions plus Python/CLI scaffolds for serving-infra, ML CI/CD, and 
eval-framework using Subtask 1 findings (API surfaces, auth, schemas, local 
tool.json conventions); (2) author nine SKILL.md files using Subtask 2 
findings, wiring each to the precise commands from existing MCPs + the three 
new tools; (3) produce a coverage matrix (skill × tool command) to confirm no
dangling references and that Responsibilities 6/7/8, SOP-1/2/3, ML Launch 
Review Checklist gates, cost stewardship, and Symphony manifest discipline are
all fully encoded; (4) verify the ML CI/CD tool does NOT duplicate bitbucket 
MCP Pipelines functionality; (5) include canonical role-doc / SPIKE / runbook
references in each artifact."
}
