## 5. PIR Template Structure (from Atlassian's Internal Standards)

Based on the research, Atlassian's PIR template (`TEMPLATE: PIR (for automation only with LLM)`) includes these mandatory sections that the `pir_drafter` tool must populate:

| Section | Content Source | Auto-fillable? |
|---------|---------------|----------------|
| Incident Summary | Reasoning traces + incident timeline | ✅ Yes |
| Timeline | Slack channel messages + timestamps | ✅ Yes |
| Impact | Metrics from monitoring + blast radius | ✅ Yes |
| Detection | Alert source + TTD timestamp | ✅ Yes |
| Response | Responder list + actions taken | ✅ Yes |
| Recovery | Mitigation steps + TTR timestamp | ✅ Yes |
| Five Whys | Reasoning traces → root cause chain | ✅ Yes (draft) |
| Root Cause | From five-whys analysis | ✅ Yes (draft) |
| Actions | Generated action items with link types | ✅ Yes |
| Incident Metrics | TTD/TTH/TTR/TTC computed from timestamps | ✅ Yes |
| Lessons | From reasoning traces | ✅ Yes (draft) |

**Incident Metrics Computation** (from TEMPLATE: PIR):
- **TTD (Time to Detect)**: Detection timestamp − Impact start timestamp. Target: < 30 minutes (previously 15 min for some teams)
- **TTH (Time to Handle)**: HOT creation timestamp − Major severity breach timestamp. Target: < 25 minutes
- **TTR/TTM (Time to Resolve/Mitigate)**: Impact end timestamp − Major severity breach timestamp. Target: < 2 hours
- **TTC (Time to Communicate)**: First comms timestamp − HOT creation timestamp. Target: < 30 minutes

**PIR Action Item Types** (link types in PIRA project):
- `PIR - TTD Action` — For detection improvement actions
- `PIR - TTR Action` — For resolution improvement actions
- `PIR - TTC Action` — For communication improvement actions (tracked from Q2-FY26)
- `PIR - HIGH PRIORITY ACTION` — SLO:56days (8 weeks)
- `PIR - MEDIUM PRIORITY ACTION` — SLO: 98 days (14 weeks)
- `PIR - LOW PRIORITY ACTION` — SLO: 140 days (20 weeks)
- `PIR - NEGOTIATED ACTION` — Negotiated with owning team

