## 7. Model Card / System Card Template

From Atlassian's `What is a System Card` page, the standard Model Card (per Google's "Model Cards for Model Reporting") includes:

| Section | Content |
|---------|---------|
| Model Details | Name, version, type, architecture, owner, date |
| Intended Use | Primary use cases, out-of-scope uses |
| Training Data | Sources, size, timeframe, preprocessing |
| Evaluation Data | Test sets, metrics |
| Performance | Metrics (precision, recall, F1), disaggregated by subgroups |
| Limitations | Known weaknesses, failure modes |
| Ethical Considerations | Bias, fairness, privacy |
| Deployment Info | Serving infrastructure, latency, capacity |

The `ML Algorithm Launch Review Template` (DTIE space) provides an internal variant:

| Section | Content |
|---------|---------|
| Project Overview | Algorithm name, date, owner, business objective, stakeholders |
| Technical Overview | Model type, evaluation metrics, benchmark/baseline, key features, training data |
| Experimentation | Offline results, online A/B results, comparison vs baseline, unexpected findings |
| Launch Execution | Rollout strategy, monitoring setup, operational readiness, business impact, operational impact |

