## 4. How This Applies to SOP-3 Skill Implementation

### 4.1 MCP Commands the AI Employee Will Invoke

#### For Channel Setup (Incident Start):
```
1. workspace_create_channel_with_members- Create #incident-{id} channel
   - Add initial responders
   
2. channel_create_message (initial status post)
   - channelId: newly created channel
   - text: Incident summary card (severity, impact, TTD, current status)
   - No threadTs (creates parent message)
```

#### For 30-Minute Cadence Updates:
```
3. channel_get_message (check last update time)
   - channelId: incident channel
   - Time range: last 30 minutes
   - Purpose: Verify whether an update has been posted

4. channel_create_message (post cadence update)
   - channelId: incident channel
   - threadTs: parent incident message timestamp (thread replies)
   - text: Formatted status update with:
     • Current status (investigating/fixing/mitigating)
     • Time elapsed since incident start
     • Actions taken since last update
     • Next planned actions• Current responders

5. channel_create_message (reminder if no update detected)
   - channelId: incident channel
   - text: "⚠️ 30-minute SLO: No status update posted in the last 30 minutes.Please post an update or acknowledge this reminder."
```

#### For Escalation/De-escalation:
```
6. workspace_search_user_by_email (resolve new responders)
   - email: responder email from on-call schedule

7. channel_users_invite (add escalated responders)
   - channelId: incident channel
   - user IDs: resolved responder IDs

8. channel_create_message (severity change notification)
   - text: "🔴 Severity escalated from Sev-2 to Sev-1. Additional responders paged."
```

#### For ActionToolAgent (Alternative Write Path):
```
ActionToolAgent:
  product: SLACK
  actionRequest: "Send message to channel #incident-{id}:
    [30-MIN UPDATE] Status: Fixing | TTR estimate: 45min | 
    Actions: Circuit breaker engaged at 14:02, investigating root cause in model serving layer"
```

### 4.2 Cadence Timer Logic (Skill-Level, Not MCP)

Since MCP tools don't include a native scheduler/timer, the cadence logic must be implemented at the **skill orchestration level**:

```
CADENCE_LOOP:
  1. Record timestamp of last status update (from channel_get_message)
  2. Calculate elapsed time since last update
  3. IF elapsed >= 30 minutes:
     a. Check if human has posted update (channel_get_message scan)
     b. IF no human update found:
        - Generate status summary from available telemetry
        - Post automated update via channel_create_message
        - Post reminder to incident commanderc. IF human update found:
        - Reset timer
        - Log compliance4. Sleep/wait until next check interval (recommend: 5-minute polling)5. GOTO CADENCE_LOOP
```

