## 7. Key Operational Patterns from Atlassian Internal Practice

### 7.1 FedRAMP RFC-0031 Cadence Requirements
- **During containment**: Updates every 2 hours
- **During remediation**: Updates every 8 hours
- **Internal (Atlassian standard)**: Updates every 30 minutes
- **Final report**: Within 5 business days of closure

**Source:** [RFC-0031 Gap Analysis](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020e5d2b5ae8ccf40ad9a2a1bbf4037fd16/pages/6900253179)

### 7.2 Multi-Channel Communication Pattern (from Integration Patterns — JSM Operations)
1. Incident created in JSM
2. Automation posts to Slack channel
3. Team can view incident details and thread
4. Slash commands allow actions (acknowledge, resolve, escalate)
5. Incident updates post to channel
6. Post-resolution summary sent to channel

**Source:** [Integration Patterns — JSM Operations](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/cdoc/pages/6649219727)

### 7.3 IMA Context-Based Reminders Pattern
IMA provides "context-based reminders" that reduce cognitive load on the Incident Commander. The AI employee should replicate this pattern:
- Reminders are **situational** (based on elapsed time + missing data)
- Reminders reference **specific missing information** (not generic nudges)
- Reminders include **direct action links** or commands

**Source:** [Manage incident restoration - Slack Channel and Zoom Room](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IMPIR/pages/3274804076)

