## 1. Available Slack MCP Tool Inventory (Read/Write)

### 1.1Rovo Dev Native Slack MCP Tools (10 tools)

| Tool | Purpose | Key Parameters | Cadence Relevance |
|------|---------|----------------|-------------------|
| `channel_create_message` | Send a message to a channel or thread | `channelId` (required), `text` (required), `threadTs` (optional) | **Primary tool** for posting cadence updates |
| `channel_get_message` | Fetch messages from a channel by ID + time range | `channelId`, time range params | Read channel state to assess what's been communicated |
| `message_get_reply` | Get thread replies for a specific message | `channelId` + message timestamp | Monitor thread activity, check if updates have been posted |
| `workspace_search_user_by_email` | Find user by email | `email` (required) | Resolve incident responders for @mentions |
| `get_user` | Get user profile (name, title) | `id` (required) | Resolve user IDs to display names |
| `channel_users_invite` | Invite users to channel | user IDs, channel ID | Add responders to incident channel |
| `workspace_create_channel_with_members` | Create channel + invite members | channel name, member IDs | Create incident channel at SOP-3 start |
| `workspace_create_empty_channel` | Create empty channel | channel name | Create incident channel scaffold |
| `slack_search_realtime` | Real-time search across workspace | supports `from:`, `in:`, `@mention`, date ranges | Search for related incident discussions, prior updates |
| `check_permission` | Check entity permissions | entity reference | Verify bot can post to target channel |

**Source:** [MCP Tools Reference: All Available Agent Tools](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120209fe3ef8486924070b8943b17f0a9782b/pages/6805853191), [(AI generated) Slack MCP Capabilities, Limitations & Workarounds](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DAT1/pages/6833693099)

### 1.2 ActionToolAgent — Slack Write Action

| Action ID | Product | What It Does | Parameters |
|-----------|---------|--------------|------------|
| `slack-send-channel-message` | SLACK | Send a message to a specific Slack channel or DM | `actionRequest` (natural language description of message + target channel) |

**How it works in practice:**
- Rovo receives intent → identifies product as `SLACK`
- Constructs structured `actionRequest` (e.g., "post message Y to channel Z")
- Calls the relevant integration API to execute
- Returns confirmation or error
- Permission-aware: can only do what the authenticated user could do manually

**Source:** [Action Tool vs Stratus Minion](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120208395a216dfb54d4cb2a4019e77122f5f/pages/6771165751), [ActionToolAgent to MCP Agent: Full Migration Audit](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120200e50839a86794972a092b418877be3af/pages/6974150473)

### 1.3 Underlying Slack Web API Methods (for reference/context)

| Method | Purpose | Rate Limit | Cadence Use |
|--------|---------|------------|-------------|
| `chat.postMessage` | Post to channel/thread | Tier 3: 1 msg/sec/channel | Primary messaging |
| `chat.scheduleMessage` | Schedule future message delivery | Standard limits | Pre-schedule cadence reminders |
| `conversations.history` | Fetch channel message history | Tier 3 | Check last update timestamp |
| `conversations.replies` | Fetch thread replies | Tier 3 | Read status thread |
| `conversations.info` | Get channel metadata | Tier 3 | Validate channel exists |

