# Bitbucket MCP Commands Relevant to SOP-1 (Drift-Triggered Retraining PRs) and SOP-3 (Production Incident Hotfixes)

## Executive Summary

This research identifies and maps all available Bitbucket MCP commands across **four distinct Bitbucket integration surfaces** at Atlassian to the two target SOPs. The findings include concrete parameter schemas, workflow sequences, autonomy tier implications, and gaps requiring new tooling.

---

## 1. Available Bitbucket MCP Integration Surfaces

### Surface A: Atlassian Rovo MCP Server (Central Server — `mcp__bitbucket__`)

This is the centralized MCP server (previously called `user-atlassian-mcp`) that exposes Bitbucket tools alongside Jira, Confluence, etc. It is the **primary surface for the AI Employee**.

**Source:** [MCP tools in Atlassian-MCP](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020f4269bb8f3da4720b0e7f63d122fb093/pages/6262617204/MCP+tools+in+Atlassian-MCP) + [Bitbucket MCP: Tool Proposal](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/mcp/pages/5563738405/Bitbucket+MCP+Tool+Proposal)

#### Create Operations
| Tool | Description | Parameters |
|------|-------------|------------|
| `createBitbucketPullRequest` | Create a new PR from source→target branch with optional reviewers & description | workspace, repo_slug, title, source_branch, destination_branch, description, reviewers[], draft |
| `createBitbucketBranch` | Create a new branch from a target commit or branch | workspace, repo_slug, name, target (commit hash or branch name) |
| `createBitbucketCommit` | Create a new commit by uploading files, optionally on a new branch | workspace, repo_slug, branch, message, files[], author |
| `createBitbucketEnvironment` | Create a new deployment environment | workspace, repo_slug, name, type, rank |

#### Get/Read Operations
| Tool | Description | Parameters |
|------|-------------|------------|
| `getBitbucketWorkspaces` | List accessible workspaces | search, filter |
| `getBitbucketRepositories` | List repos in a workspace | workspace, search, sort |
| `getBitbucketRepository` | Get repo details + default branch | workspace, repo_slug |
| `getBitbucketPullRequest` | Get PR details (status, reviewers, comments) | workspace, repo_slug, pull_request_id |
| `getBitbucketPullRequests` | List PRs filtered by state | workspace, repo_slug, state (OPEN/MERGED/DECLINED) |
| `getBitbucketPullRequestDiff` | Get the diff/changes of a PR | workspace, repo_slug, pull_request_id |
| `getBitbucketBranch` | Get branch details + latest commit | workspace, repo_slug, branch_name |
| `getBitbucketCommit` | Get commit details | workspace, repo_slug, commit_hash |
| `getBitbucketFileContents` | Get file/directory contents at a commit/branch/tag | workspace, repo_slug, path, commit |
| `getBitbucketPipelines` | List pipelines (filtered by branch, commit, status, trigger) | workspace, repo_slug, filters |
| `getBitbucketPipeline` | Get specific pipeline execution details | workspace, repo_slug, pipeline_uuid |
| `getBitbucketPipelineSteps` | List all steps in a pipeline | workspace, repo_slug, pipeline_uuid |
| `getBitbucketPipelineStep` | Get step details | workspace, repo_slug, pipeline_uuid, step_uuid |
| `getBitbucketPipelineStepLog` | Get log output for a pipeline step | workspace, repo_slug, pipeline_uuid, step_uuid |
| `getBitbucketDeployments` | List deployments (filtered by env, state) | workspace, repo_slug, environment, state |
| `getBitbucketDeployment` | Get deployment details | workspace, repo_slug, deployment_uuid |
| `getBitbucketEnvironments` | List configured environments | workspace, repo_slug |

#### Update/Write Operations
| Tool | Description | Parameters |
|------|-------------|------------|
| `mergeBitbucketPullRequest` | Merge a PR with strategy options | workspace, repo_slug, pull_request_id, merge_strategy, close_source_branch |
| `approveBitbucketPullRequest` | Approve a PR | workspace, repo_slug, pull_request_id |
| `addBitbucketPullRequestComment` | Add a comment to a PR | workspace, repo_slug, pull_request_id, content |
| `runBitbucketPipeline` | Trigger a pipeline on branch/commit with variables | workspace, repo_slug, target.ref_name, target.ref_type, target.selector, variables[] |
| `updateBitbucketEnvironment` | Update environment name/type/rank | workspace, repo_slug, environment_uuid, name, type, rank |

---

### Surface B: `@atlassian/bitbucket-mcp-server` (Standalone NPM Package —21Tools)

This is the externally-published Bitbucket-specific MCP server with **enhanced tooling** beyond the centralized server.

**Source:** [Bitbucket MCP Server — Complete Features & Functionality Reference](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~63466dc525e69efe130150e4/pages/6475679720/Bitbucket+MCP+Server+Complete+Features+Functionality+Reference)

**Additional tools beyond Surface A:**
| Tool | Description | Relevance |
|------|-------------|-----------|
| `search_pull_requests` | Advanced search with branch/state/author/date/title filters | **SOP-1**: Find existing retraining PRs; **SOP-3**: Find open hotfix PRs |
| `list_previous_pull_requests` | Merged PR history for a repo | **SOP-1**: Check if retraining PR already exists for a model |
| `get_default_reviewers` | Fetch repo's default reviewers (UUID format) | **SOP-1/3**: Auto-assign correct reviewers |
| `get_pull_request_comments` | All comments with resolution status | **SOP-3**: Check reviewer feedback on hotfix |
| `get_pull_request_changes` | Full diff with path/whitespace/context control | **SOP-3**: Validate hotfix scope is minimal |
| `get_build_status` | Latest pipeline runs (max 30) for a branch, highlighting failures | **SOP-1/3**: Gate merge on green pipeline |
| `get_pipeline_details` | Deep analysis: steps, test reports, logs for failures | **SOP-1/3**: Diagnose pipeline failures |
| `run_pipeline` | Full pipeline trigger with selector/variables/commit targeting | **SOP-1**: Trigger retraining pipeline; **SOP-3**: Trigger hotfix pipeline |

---

### Surface C: RovoFlow Bitbucket Commands (Workflow Automation)

These are used in YAML-based RovoFlow workflows and provide a higher-level abstraction.

**Source:** [Bitbucket Commands](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~28680196/pages/6638559794/Bitbucket+Commands)

| Command | Description | Parameters |
|---------|-------------|------------|
| `bitbucket.get_client` | Establish connection to Stash or Bitbucket Cloud | target: "stash" \| "bitbucket_cloud" |
| `bitbucket.open_pull_request` | Create PR between two branches | client, title, source_branch, destination_branch, description |
| `bitbucket.add_pull_request_comment` | Add comment to PR | client, pull_request_id, text |
| `bitbucket.add_pull_request_reviewers` | Assign multiple reviewers | client, pull_request_id, users[] |
| `bitbucket.add_pull_request_task` | Add blocker/task comment | client, pull_request_id, task |
| `bitbucket.update_pull_request_task` | Resolve/open a task | client, pull_request_id, task_id, state ("OPEN"/"RESOLVED"), version |
| `bitbucket.get_pull_request_tasks` | List all tasks on PR | client, pull_request_id |
| `bitbucket.get_pull_request` | Get PR details | client, pull_request_id |
| `bitbucket.get_pull_requests_by_filter` | Filter PRs by state/author/target branch | client, state_filter, author_filter, target_filter, limits |
| `bitbucket.decline_pull_request` | Reject/close a PR | client, pull_request_id, version |

**Context variables required:** `bitbucket_project_key`, `bitbucket_repository_slug`, `bitbucket_client_name`

---

### Surface D: Agentic Pipelines Built-in MCP (In-Pipeline Agent Access)

When running inside Bitbucket Pipelines (Agentic Pipelines), agents have access to a built-in Bitbucket Cloud MCP server.

**Source:** [Interacting with Bitbucket via MCP (official docs)](https://support.atlassian.com/bitbucket-cloud/docs/interacting-with-bitbucket-via-mcp/)

| Tool | Description | Scope Required |
|------|-------------|---------------|
| `createPullRequest` | Create a new PR | write:pullrequest:bitbucket |
| `getPullRequests` | List PRs | read:pullrequest:bitbucket |
| `getPullRequestDetails` | Fetch PR details | read:pullrequest:bitbucket |
| `getPullRequestComments` | List PR comments | read:pullrequest:bitbucket |
| `addPullRequestComment` | Add a comment (general or inline) | write:pullrequest:bitbucket |
| `updatePullRequestComment` | Edit agent-created comment | write:pullrequest:bitbucket |
| `getPullRequestTasks` | List tasks on PR | read:pullrequest:bitbucket |
| `createPullRequestTask` | Add a task | write:pullrequest:bitbucket |
| `updatePullRequestTask` | Update task state | write:pullrequest:bitbucket |
| `analyzePullRequestCommitStatusFailures` | Analyze failed commit statuses | read:pullrequest + read:pipeline |
| `analyzePipelineStepFailure` | Analyze why a step failed | read:pipeline:bitbucket |

---

## 2. SOP-1: Drift-Triggered Retraining — Bitbucket MCP Command Mapping

### Workflow Steps → Command Mapping

| SOP-1 Step | Autonomy | Bitbucket MCP Commands | Notes |
|------------|----------|------------------------|-------|
| **Step 4: Create retraining branch** | 🟢 Auto | `createBitbucketBranch(workspace, repo_slug, name="retrain/{model_name}-{date}", target="main")` | Naming convention: `retrain/{model}-{YYYYMMDD}` |
| **Step 5: Commit config/data changes** | 🟢 Auto | `createBitbucketCommit(workspace, repo_slug, branch="retrain/...", message="chore(ml): trigger retraining for {model} — drift detected", files=[...])` | Files: updated training config YAML, drift report, thresholds |
| **Step 6: Trigger retraining pipeline** | 🟡 Confirm | `runBitbucketPipeline(workspace, repo_slug, target.ref_name="retrain/...", target.ref_type="branch", target.selector.type="custom", target.selector.pattern="retrain", variables=[{key:"MODEL_NAME", value:...}, {key:"DRIFT_METRICS", value:...}])` | Custom pipeline selector; variables pass model context |
| **Step 7: Monitor pipeline** | 🟢 Auto | `getBitbucketPipelines(workspace, repo_slug, branch="retrain/...")` → `getBitbucketPipelineSteps(...)` → `getBitbucketPipelineStepLog(...)` | Poll until COMPLETED/FAILED; extract test results |
| **Step 8: Open retraining PR** | 🟡 Confirm | `createBitbucketPullRequest(workspace, repo_slug, title="[ML Retrain] {model_name} — drift-triggered", source="retrain/...", destination="main", description="{drift_report + eval_results}", reviewers=[...])` | Description includes drift metrics, before/after eval scores |
| **Step 8a: Add default reviewers** | 🟢 Auto | `get_default_reviewers(workspace, repo_slug)` (Surface B) OR hardcoded team list | Auto-assign ML team reviewers |
| **Step 8b: Add PR task for eval gate** | 🟢 Auto | `addBitbucketPullRequestComment(workspace, repo_slug, pr_id, "## Retraining Evaluation Results\n...")` | Structured comment with metrics table |
| **Step 9: Verify pipeline passes** | 🟢 Auto | `get_build_status(workspace, repo_slug, branch="retrain/...")` OR `getBitbucketPipelines(...)` | Gate: all checks green before requesting merge |
| **Step 9a: Check for conflicts** | 🟢 Auto | `getBitbucketPullRequest(workspace, repo_slug, pr_id)` → check `merge_status` | Verify PR is mergeable |

### Key Observations for SOP-1:
- **No `decline_pull_request`** exposed on Surface A — need Surface C's `bitbucket.decline_pull_request` if retraining fails evaluation
- **No file-level commit** for updating model artifacts (large files) — may need external artifact store (ML Registry/Tarot) with Bitbucket only tracking config
- **Pipeline variables** are critical for passing drift context to the retraining job
- **Search for existing PRs** (`search_pull_requests` on Surface B with `source_branch` filter on "retrain/") prevents duplicate PR creation

---

## 3. SOP-3: Production Incident Hotfix — Bitbucket MCP Command Mapping

### Workflow Steps → Command Mapping

Based on the [Runbook: Hotfix pipeline](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ECO/pages/6949808627/Runbook+Hotfix+pipeline) and [ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/6058351626/ML-Engine+Circuit+Breaker+Runbook):

| SOP-3 Step | Autonomy | Bitbucket MCP Commands | Notes |
|------------|----------|------------------------|-------|
| **Step 1: Identify fix commit** | 🟡 Confirm | `getBitbucketCommit(workspace, repo_slug, commit_hash)` + `getBitbucketFileContents(workspace, repo_slug, path, commit)` | Locate the fix commit on main or write new fix |
| **Step 2: Create hotfix branch** | 🟢 Auto | `createBitbucketBranch(workspace, repo_slug, name="fix/{HOT-XXXX}-{description}", target="hotfix")` | **CRITICAL**: Branch from `hotfix` not `main` per runbook |
| **Step 3: Apply fix (cherry-pick or new)** | 🔴 Human | `createBitbucketCommit(workspace, repo_slug, branch="fix/...", message="fix({service}): {description} [HOT-XXXX]", files=[...])` | For net-new fixes only; cherry-picks need git CLI |
| **Step 4: Push and create PR → hotfix** | 🟡 Confirm | `createBitbucketPullRequest(workspace, repo_slug, title="[HOTFIX] HOT-{id}: {description}", source="fix/HOT-...", destination="hotfix", description="## Incident\n{HOT link}\n## Fix\n{description}\n## Validation\n{test_plan}")` | **CRITICAL**: Target branch must be `hotfix`, NOT `main` |
| **Step 4a: Add reviewers** | 🟢 Auto | `get_default_reviewers(workspace, repo_slug)` OR on-call assignee | Expedited review from second on-call engineer |
| **Step 4b: Add PR comment with context** | 🟢 Auto | `addBitbucketPullRequestComment(workspace, repo_slug, pr_id, "## Incident Context\nHOT: ...\nCircuit Breaker State: ...\nImpact: ...\n\n## Change Scope Validation\n- [ ] Only intended change\n- [ ] Target branch is `hotfix`\n- [ ] Tests pass")` | Links to incident, CB state, scope checklist |
| **Step 5: Monitor PR pipeline** | 🟢 Auto | `getBitbucketPipelines(workspace, repo_slug, branch="fix/...")` → `getBitbucketPipelineSteps(...)` → `getBitbucketPipelineStepLog(...)` | Wait for tests + lint + poco + desloppify |
| **Step 5a: Analyze pipeline failure** | 🟢 Auto | `get_pipeline_details(workspace, repo_slug, pipeline_id)` OR `analyzePipelineStepFailure(...)` (Surface D) | Auto-diagnose: test report, stack traces, log lines |
| **Step 6: Merge hotfix PR** | 🔴 Human | `mergeBitbucketPullRequest(workspace, repo_slug, pr_id, merge_strategy="merge-commit", close_source_branch=true)` | Requires human approval first; triggers hotfix pipeline |
| **Step 7: Monitor deployment pipeline** | 🟢 Auto | `getBitbucketPipelines(workspace, repo_slug, branch="hotfix")` → latest pipeline → `getBitbucketPipelineSteps(...)` | Watch: build → Docker image → Spinnaker trigger |
| **Step 8: Post-incident sync** | 🟡 Confirm | `createBitbucketBranch(workspace, repo_slug, name="chore/sync-hotfix-to-main", target="main")` → `createBitbucketPullRequest(workspace, repo_slug, title="chore: sync hotfix to main [HOT-XXXX]", source="chore/sync-hotfix-to-main", destination="main", description="...")` | Cherry-pick or merge `hotfix`→`main` |
| **Step 9(Rollback): Revert** | 🔴 Human | Same PR flow but with revert commit: `createBitbucketBranch(...)` → `createBitbucketCommit(...)` → `createBitbucketPullRequest(...)` targeting `hotfix` | Revert commit on hotfix branch |

### Circuit Breaker Integration (via Switcheroo MCP):
The ML-Engine Circuit Breaker is controlled via Switcheroo feature gate `aiops_circuit_breaker_enabled`:

| Action | Switcheroo MCP Command | Notes |
|--------|----------------------|-------|
| Check CB state | `search_changes(search="aiops_circuit_breaker")` → `get_change_details(changeId)` | Read gate status, rollout%, lifecycle |
| Check CB changelog | `search_changelog(changeId=..., startDate=..., endDate=...)` | Who changed what and when during incident window |

**Gap identified**: No Switcheroo MCP command currently supports **toggling a gate** (enable/disable/rollout %). Per the [Switcheroo MCP Engineering Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202086518f487b04434b9244ecf84b9a34b4/pages/6873894402/Switcheroo+MCP+Server+Engineering+Plan): "Transitions (launching, rolling out, rolling back) and rule changes are high-risk and should remain deliberate human actions." This means the `circuit_breaker_control` tool in the AI Employee spec **must wrap direct Switcheroo REST API calls** rather than existing MCP commands:
- `POST /api/v2/switcheroo/gate/{id}/rollout` (proposed, not yet exposed)
- Or direct Switcheroo UI URL generation for human confirmation

