## 3. SOP-3: Production Incident Hotfix — Bitbucket MCP Command Mapping

### Workflow Steps → Command Mapping

Based on the [Runbook: Hotfix pipeline](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ECO/pages/6949808627/Runbook+Hotfix+pipeline) and [ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/6058351626/ML-Engine+Circuit+Breaker+Runbook):

| SOP-3 Step | Autonomy | Bitbucket MCP Commands | Notes |
|------------|----------|------------------------|-------|
| **Step 1: Identify fix commit** | 🟡 Confirm | `getBitbucketCommit(workspace, repo_slug, commit_hash)` + `getBitbucketFileContents(workspace, repo_slug, path, commit)` | Locate the fix commit on main or write new fix |
| **Step 2: Create hotfix branch** | 🟢 Auto | `createBitbucketBranch(workspace, repo_slug, name="fix/{HOT-XXXX}-{description}", target="hotfix")` | **CRITICAL**: Branch from `hotfix` not `main` per runbook |
| **Step 3: Apply fix (cherry-pick or new)** | 🔴 Human | `createBitbucketCommit(workspace, repo_slug, branch="fix/...", message="fix({service}): {description} [HOT-XXXX]", files=[...])` | For net-new fixes only; cherry-picks need git CLI |
| **Step 4: Push and create PR → hotfix** | 🟡 Confirm | `createBitbucketPullRequest(workspace, repo_slug, title="[HOTFIX] HOT-{id}: {description}", source="fix/HOT-...", destination="hotfix", description="## Incident\n{HOT link}\n## Fix\n{description}\n## Validation\n{test_plan}")` | **CRITICAL**: Target branch must be `hotfix`, NOT `main` |
| **Step 4a: Add reviewers** | 🟢 Auto | `get_default_reviewers(workspace, repo_slug)` OR on-call assignee | Expedited review from second on-call engineer |
| **Step 4b: Add PR comment with context** | 🟢 Auto | `addBitbucketPullRequestComment(workspace, repo_slug, pr_id, "## Incident Context\nHOT: ...\nCircuit Breaker State: ...\nImpact: ...\n\n## Change Scope Validation\n- [ ] Only intended change\n- [ ] Target branch is `hotfix`\n- [ ] Tests pass")` | Links to incident, CB state, scope checklist |
| **Step 5: Monitor PR pipeline** | 🟢 Auto | `getBitbucketPipelines(workspace, repo_slug, branch="fix/...")` → `getBitbucketPipelineSteps(...)` → `getBitbucketPipelineStepLog(...)` | Wait for tests + lint + poco + desloppify |
| **Step 5a: Analyze pipeline failure** | 🟢 Auto | `get_pipeline_details(workspace, repo_slug, pipeline_id)` OR `analyzePipelineStepFailure(...)` (Surface D) | Auto-diagnose: test report, stack traces, log lines |
| **Step 6: Merge hotfix PR** | 🔴 Human | `mergeBitbucketPullRequest(workspace, repo_slug, pr_id, merge_strategy="merge-commit", close_source_branch=true)` | Requires human approval first; triggers hotfix pipeline |
| **Step 7: Monitor deployment pipeline** | 🟢 Auto | `getBitbucketPipelines(workspace, repo_slug, branch="hotfix")` → latest pipeline → `getBitbucketPipelineSteps(...)` | Watch: build → Docker image → Spinnaker trigger |
| **Step 8: Post-incident sync** | 🟡 Confirm | `createBitbucketBranch(workspace, repo_slug, name="chore/sync-hotfix-to-main", target="main")` → `createBitbucketPullRequest(workspace, repo_slug, title="chore: sync hotfix to main [HOT-XXXX]", source="chore/sync-hotfix-to-main", destination="main", description="...")` | Cherry-pick or merge `hotfix`→`main` |
| **Step 9(Rollback): Revert** | 🔴 Human | Same PR flow but with revert commit: `createBitbucketBranch(...)` → `createBitbucketCommit(...)` → `createBitbucketPullRequest(...)` targeting `hotfix` | Revert commit on hotfix branch |

### Circuit Breaker Integration (via Switcheroo MCP):
The ML-Engine Circuit Breaker is controlled via Switcheroo feature gate `aiops_circuit_breaker_enabled`:

| Action | Switcheroo MCP Command | Notes |
|--------|----------------------|-------|
| Check CB state | `search_changes(search="aiops_circuit_breaker")` → `get_change_details(changeId)` | Read gate status, rollout%, lifecycle |
| Check CB changelog | `search_changelog(changeId=..., startDate=..., endDate=...)` | Who changed what and when during incident window |

**Gap identified**: No Switcheroo MCP command currently supports **toggling a gate** (enable/disable/rollout %). Per the [Switcheroo MCP Engineering Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202086518f487b04434b9244ecf84b9a34b4/pages/6873894402/Switcheroo+MCP+Server+Engineering+Plan): "Transitions (launching, rolling out, rolling back) and rule changes are high-risk and should remain deliberate human actions." This means the `circuit_breaker_control` tool in the AI Employee spec **must wrap direct Switcheroo REST API calls** rather than existing MCP commands:
- `POST /api/v2/switcheroo/gate/{id}/rollout` (proposed, not yet exposed)
- Or direct Switcheroo UI URL generation for human confirmation

---

## 4. Gaps vs. Existing MCP Surface — Commands Needed but Not Available

| Required Capability | SOP | Gap Type | Proposed Resolution |
|--------------------|----|----------|---------------------|
| **Cherry-pick commit** from one branch to another | SOP-3 | Missing — no git-level rebase/cherry-pick via API | Use `createBitbucketCommit` with the file contents from the source commit; or require git CLI step |
| **Decline/close PR** | SOP-1 (failed eval) | Missing on Surface A | Available on Surface C (`bitbucket.decline_pull_request`); add to tool surface |
| **Get PR merge status/conflicts** | SOP-1/3 | Partial — must parse from `getBitbucketPullRequest` response | No dedicated endpoint; parse `merge_status` field from PR details |
| **Trigger pipeline with inline YAML** (on-demand pipeline) | SOP-1 edge case | Not exposed via MCP | Available via REST API (`Content-Type: application/yaml`); may not be needed for standard custom pipelines |
| **Toggle Switcheroo gate** (circuit breaker on/off) | SOP-3 | Not exposed via any MCP | Need custom `circuit_breaker_control` tool wrapping Switcheroo REST + mandatory human confirmation |
| **Search commits on a branch** (for finding fix commit) | SOP-3 | Not on Surface A | Available via REST API `GET /2.0/repositories/{w}/{r}/commits?include={branch}` — propose adding to tool surface |
| **Get PR approval count/status** | SOP-1/3 | Embedded in `getBitbucketPullRequest` response | Parse `participants` array for `approved: true` entries |
| **Upload large model artifacts** | SOP-1| Fundamental limitation | Use ML Registry (Tarot) for model artifacts; Bitbucket for config/code only |

