Local artifact survey: Worker context dirs were empty; only
~/.agents/skills/twg exists. The 1A tool is net-new — recommend following the
twg skill layout (SKILL.md + scripts/ + references/).

Launchpad (authoritative sources: AO2/6025226094 + MLP/5834564444):

 • SDK: pip install atlassian-msp-sdk (v0.9+); entry from 
   atlassian_msp_sdk.clients.launchpad.endpoint_ts import launch_to_teamserve.
 • Endpoint object methods: get_endpoint_details(), info(), logs() (Splunk),
   metrics() (SignalFx), invoke(body, content_type), delete().
 • HTTP contract: Deploy/Invoke/Delete/Describe. Deploy body = instance,
   container, envVars, endpointName, tarotComponentRef, tarotVersionRef,
   tags[], expiry (epoch ms). Invoke at teamserve/launchpad/.
 • TTL defaults 2h (must enforce). Stateless service → poll Describe.status.
 • Error taxonomy: LaunchpadUnavailableError (retry w/ backoff), RequestError
   4xx (no retry), LaunchpadFailureError 5xx (retry once → escalate). Support:
   #help-launchpad-ts.

SageMaker / MSP (authoritative: 3907418837 + Bluebird scoping):

 • Prod path goes through sagemaker-osb orchestrated by Spinnaker; declarative
   scaling: block in Micros sd.yml (min/max/instance/threshold/cooldown, or
   full custom metrics: block).
 • Resource types: sm-endpoint, sm-mc-endpoint, sm-mm-endpoint (default metric
   SageMakerVariantInvocationsPerInstance, threshold 180); sm-async
   (ApproximateBacklogSizePerInstance, threshold 5).
 • Scale-out trigger: 3 breaches in 3 min; scale-in: below threshold for 15
   min; instance availability ~5–6 min; GPU instances currently constrained.
 • Raw boto3 wrap targets for the tool:
   sagemaker.{Describe,Update,Delete}Endpoint (+ UpdateEndpoint
   BlueGreenUpdatePolicy/RollbackConfiguration for canary/shadow/rollback),
   sagemaker-runtime.InvokeEndpoint[Async],
   application-autoscaling.{Register,PutScalingPolicy,Describe*},
   cloudwatch.{GetMetricData,PutMetricAlarm}.

Cross-cutting findings:

 • Model Service vs Deployment Instance distinction (MLP/6122166900); reads
   should go through Dreamcatcher/ML Registry, not bypass to AWS.
 • Gaps requiring new tool logic: unified cross-provider canary/shadow
   primitive, orchestrated rollback, autoscaling dry-run, GPU-availability
   pre-flight, TTL guardrails.
 • Tool↔Tool integration: 1A emits sd.yml patches and hands off to 1B
   (Spinnaker/Micros — no duplication); 1A blocks on EndpointStatus=InService
   then triggers 1C eval-gate; 1C can signal 1A to auto-rollback via stored
   EndpointConfigName.
 • Autonomy: read ops fully autonomous; Launchpad ephemeral deploys autonomous
   (TTL bounded); any UpdateEndpoint, sd.yml edit, or live min/max bump in
   prod = confirmation required + dry-run summary.

Recommended action namespaces: serving.launchpad.*, serving.sagemaker.* (+
.autoscale.*), serving.teamserve.*, serving.aigateway.*, serving.lineage.*,
serving.health.


