## 5. SOP-3 Workflow: What the AI Employee Can Do TODAY

### 5.1 Incident Investigation (Fully Automated via MCP)

```
Step 1: Identify potential faulty gates
  Tool: search_changelog
  Parameters: {
    "limit": 20,
    "timeFilters": { "lastXHoursTimePreset": 2 },
    "targetApps": ["<affected-service>_server"]
  }

Step 2: Get details on suspicious gate
  Tool: get_change_details
  Parameters: { "changeId": "<id-from-step-1>" }

Step 3: Search for circuit breaker gates
  Tool: search_changes
  Parameters: {
    "query": "circuit_breaker",
    "targetApps": ["<affected-service>_server"],
    "kinds": ["feature_gate"]
  }
```

### 5.2 Circuit Breaker Activation (REQUIRES HUMAN — No MCP Write Tool)

**Current state:** The AI employee CANNOT programmatically toggle/pause/disable a gate via MCP. It must:
1. Identify the gate to toggle (automated via `search_changes` + `get_change_details`)
2. Provide the human with a **direct Switcheroo UI link** for manual toggle
3. Alternatively, provide the `atlas sre statsig` CLI command for the on-call engineer

**Link format:** `https://switcheroo.atlassian.com/ui/gates/<changeId>/key/<gateName>`

### 5.3 Future State (When Lifecycle API is Implemented)

```
Step: Activate circuit breaker (pause gate)
  Tool: lifecycle_transition (future)
  Endpoint: PATCH /api/v2/switcheroo/gate/{changeId}/lifecycle
  Body: {
    "targetState": "paused",
    "reason": "HOT-XXXXX: [Auto-generated incident description]"
  }
```

