                  Highlights for the Serving-infra tool (1A)

                               Endpoint pattern

 • gRPC: grpc-teamserve-{region}.{env}.services.kitt-inf.net:443 (regions:
   us-east-1, us-west-2, eu-west-1, apse1/2; envs: dev/stg/prod).
 • HTTP:
   teamserve-{region}.{env}.services.kitt-inf.net/v1/models/{source}/{group}/v
   ersions/{version}/v2/models/{name}/infer (Triton) or /v1/chat/completions
   (vLLM).
 • gRPC model selection is header-based (not subpath): x-teamserve-source,
   x-teamserve-model, x-teamserve-model-version.

                                    Protos

 • No Atlassian-proprietary proto. Inference uses upstream NVIDIA Triton
   grpc_service.proto (ServerLive, ServerReady, ModelReady, ModelMetadata,
   ModelConfig, ModelInfer, ModelStreamInfer, ModelStatistics, plus
   RepositoryModelLoad/Unload only when --model-control-mode=EXPLICIT).
 • Canonical client reference: PR atlassian/conversational-ai-platform#21735
   with a three-layer pattern (TritonGrpcClient → TeamserveGrpcClient →
   per-model facade).

                                  Auth model

 • ASAP JWT (Authorization: Bearer …) verified by SLAuth, authorized via POCO
   policy per model. Each model's POCO data.json/test.json allowlists specific
   ASAP issuers (micros/<svc>). UCT carried separately for tenancy. Regional
   EnvoyFilter + AuthorizationPolicy enforce cross-region blocking
   (defense-in-depth).

                        Control plane (teamserve-api)

 • REST/JSON, lives in control-plane cluster (d6k7 dev). Key endpoints:
    • POST /api/v1/model-deployment/launch, PUT .../update (hot-swap, GPU
      reused), GET .../status/{id}, GET .../list, POST .../destroy, POST 
      .../set-expiry/{id}.
    • POST /api/v1/loadtest/{launch-and-loadtest,standalone-loadtest}.
    • GET /api/v1/model-monitor/{endpoint}[/{region}] — only prod-safe read 
      API (status, capacity, instance_type, replicas).
 • /model-deployment/* is closed off in prod — prod deploys go through PR →
   main pipeline (ML Registry register + image sync + Terraform) → ArgoCD
   App-of-Apps → Karpenter → init-container model-importer → vLLM/Triton load
   → Pollinator. Total ~26–36 min merge-to-ready.

                            Canary/shadow/rollback

 • No first-class TEAMServe canary CRD. Composed via:
    • KITT++ Progressive Rollout through Spinnaker → KDA
      (CreateDeployment/CreateRollback) → ArgoCD Rollout.
    • App-level Shadow/Ramp/Cutover done at the calling service (TEAMServe
      just hosts both versions).
 • Tool must orchestrate Spinnaker REST + KDA + ArgoCD + bitbucket-MCP PR;
   cannot bypass PRGB for prod.

                             Health & autoscaling

 • Health sources: Triton ServerReady/ModelReady, vLLM /health, kubectl get 
   app, Pollinator, model-monitor.
 • HPA + Karpenter NodePool are PR-edited. Per-deployment default resources: 2
   CPU / 8 GiB / 1 GPU / 50 GiB ephemeral.

                           Local skills/tools tree

 • Only /Users/tchen7/.agents/skills/twg/SKILL.md exists. No TEAMServe 
   tool.json to model from. Recommend skills/teamserve/{SKILL.md, tool.json, 
   scripts/teamserve}.

                                     Gaps

 1 No canary CRD inside TEAMServe (cross-tool).
 2 Prod write-API closed → must use PR path.
 3 Three x-teamserve-* headers not enforced at proto layer (footgun).
 4 Regional EnvoyFilter still rolling out — fail-closed client-side.
 5 model-monitor lacks autoscaling/rollout-history surface.
 6 Platform does no inference retry — tool must implement.

                              AI-employee notes

 • Autonomous: all read verbs + ephemeral dev
   launch/update/destroy/extend/loadtest (if agent has scoped ASAP issuer).
 • Human-gated: canary.{start,promote}, rollback, scale (Spinnaker manual
   judgment or PRGB).
 • Retry: gRPC standard codes with bounded backoff; control plane has typed
   errors (LaunchpadUnavailableError, RequestError 4xx no-retry,
   LaunchpadFailureError 5xx one-retry).

                         Recommended tool.json verbs


list, describe, health, invoke, launch, update, destroy, extend, loadtest, 
canary.{start,promote,abort}, rollback, scale, logs, metrics, model-config, 
model-stats.
