## 8. Authentication & Access Model

For the AI employee (agent context):

| Token Type | Products | How Compass Is Accessed |
|------------|----------|------------------------|
| `uct` (session) | Compass, Goals, TWG | Via AGG GraphQL gateway; no scopes needed for session |
| OAuth 2.1 | Compass (external MCP) | Requires `read:component:compass` scope |
| API Token | Compass (external MCP) | Requires `read:component:compass` scope |

The Compass MCP binding uses the GraphQL backend (`compass-gateway`), so the agent needs session-based access (for internal Rovo agent) or OAuth scopes (for external MCP clients).

**Source**: [Rovo MCP V2 Technical Architecture](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/mcp/pages/6797989483/Rovo+MCP+V2+Technical+Architecture)

