## 9. Gaps & Considerations for Skill Design

### 9.1 Existing Capabilities (Can Reuse Directly)
- ✅ Service search by name, team, type, labels
- ✅ Owner team lookup (team ARI → team name)
- ✅ On-call schedule with current responders
- ✅ Dependency graph (OUTWARD and INWARD)
- ✅ Linked documents/runbooks
- ✅ Deployment and incident event history
- ✅ Custom fields (including FinOps metadata)
- ✅ Component tier information

### 9.2 Gaps That Need New Tools or Workarounds
- ❌ **No direct "who is on-call RIGHT NOW for service X" API** that returns a single person with contact info — must compose from `includeOnCallSchedules=true` + interpret schedule data
- ❌ **Team member contact details** (email, Slack handle) not directly in Compass — need TWG `get:team-users` then people lookup
- ❌ **Cost metrics/usage data** not in Compass — need separateFinOps dashboards/Databricks queries
- ❌ **Migration status tracking** (SageMaker→TEAMServe) not native to Compass — would be custom field or Jira epic
- ❌ **Real-time alerting state** (is service currently alerting?) — need JSM Ops API, not Compass

### 9.3 Compass Deprecation Context
- Compass catalog → moving to DX platform (long term)
- Compass Operations (Alerts/On-Call) → migrating to JSM (available now)
- For the AI employee skill design, build an abstraction layer that can pivot between Compass and JSM for on-call data
- FinOps metadata may move to Service Central — design the cost skill to be metadata-source-agnostic

