# ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook — Complete Research Findings for SOP-3 Encoding

## 1. Primary Source: ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook (Full Content)

**Source**: [ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/6058351626/ML-Engine+Circuit+Breaker+Runbook)  
**Author**: Lubhani Agarwal  
**Last Modified**: 2025-11-06

### 1.1 Purpose & Scope
The runbook documents the circuit breaker (CB) added for ML-Engine. It is optimized for **on-call response, fast diagnosis, and safe remediation**. All links are inline cards and ready-to-click.

### 1.2 What the CB Protects
- Prevents cascading failures when ML-Engine or its downstream dependencies become unhealthy
- Reduces wasted retries
- Protects upstream queues from runaway backlog
- Provides a controlled recovery path via half-open probes

### 1.3 At-a-Glance Status
- Production CB: **Enabled**
- Alerting: **Active**
- Runbook: **Reviewed**

### 1.4 Quick Links (Critical for SOP-3 Tooling)
- **Switcheroo Feature Gate**: `https://switcheroo.atlassian.com/ui/gates/14ae760c-ba0f-4f8f-a62d-1ecd169737f1/key/aiops_circuit_breaker_enabled`
- **Splunk Alert**: `https://splunk.paas-inf.net/en-GB/app/search/alert?s=...Circuit%20Breaker%20State%20%3A%20Open...`
- **Design Page**: Circuit Breaker: Ml-engine & Firebolt (linked from runbook)

### 1.5 How It Works (State Machine)
- **Sliding window** observes recent calls and failure rate to decide state transitions
- **Open state** blocks calls to prevent overload
- **Half-open** allows limited probes to verify recovery
- **Closed** resumes normal traffic
- Only **5xx responses** are treated as failures (client errors do NOT trip the CB)

### 1.6 Configuration Parameters (Production Values)

| Parameter | Value / Description |
|-----------|-------------------|
| slidingWindowType | TIME_BASED |
| slidingWindowSize | 60 seconds rolling window |
| minimumNumberOfCalls | 20 (evaluate only if call count ≥ 20) |
| failureRateThreshold | 20% (CB opens if failure rate ≥ 20%) |
| waitDurationInOpenState | 30s base (exponential backoff up to max) |
| permittedNumberOfCallsInHalfOpenState | 20 (trial probes) |
| automaticTransitionFromOpenToHalfOpenEnabled | true |
| exponentialBackoffMultiplier / maxOpenWait | 2.0 multiplier; max 60s |
| recordFailurePredicate | Counts only 5xx errors as failures |

### 1.7 Operational Playbooks

#### Playbook 1: CB Tripped (Open State) — Immediate Response
1. Validate alert context in Splunk and confirm state transitions (open → half-open → closed)
2. Inspect ML-Engine 5xx errors: rate, top error codes, and impacted endpoints/models
3. Check downstream health (latency, saturation, error budgets)
4. If impact is high and outage is confirmed, consider temporarily **disabling CB for unaffected tenants via feature gate targeting** (Switcheroo). Document rationale.

#### Playbook 2: Frequent CB Trips — Pattern Analysis
1. Correlate trips with traffic spikes, model deployments, or dependency incidents
2. Review error taxonomy to ensure only true server faults (5xx) count as failures
3. Evaluate thresholds: raise minimumNumberOfCalls or failureRateThreshold if overly sensitive; lower if missing real outages

#### Playbook 3: Tuning and Safe Changes
1. Propose change with expected impact and rollback plan. Add approvers: [Tech Lead], [SRE], [Product Manager]
2. Rollout using canary: enable new thresholds for5–10% traffic, monitor for two windows of stability
3. If healthy, ramp to100% and record evidence in change notes

### 1.8 Troubleshooting Guide

| Symptom | Meaning | Action |
|---------|---------|--------|
| Many "Call not permitted" logs | CB is open; all calls short-circuited | Investigate recent5xx bursts and dependent service health; watch for half-open recovery |
| Repeated open/close flapping | Thresholds too sensitive or dependency instability | Increase minimumNumberOfCalls and/or failureRateThreshold; consider longer waitDurationInOpenState |
| CB never trips during clear outages | Thresholds too lenient or failure predicate misclassified | Lower thresholds; verify5xx mapping; ensure minimumNumberOfCalls not blocking evaluation |

### 1.9 Sample Configuration Snippet

```yaml
resilience4j.circuitbreaker:
  instances:
    ml-engine:
      slidingWindowType: TIME_BASED
      slidingWindowSize: 60
      minimumNumberOfCalls: 20
      failureRateThreshold: 20
      waitDurationInOpenState: 30s
      permittedNumberOfCallsInHalfOpenState: 20
      automaticTransitionFromOpenToHalfOpenEnabled: true
      maxWaitDurationInOpenState: 60s
      exponentialBackoffMultiplier: 2.0
      recordFailurePredicate: com.example.cb.ServerErrorOnlyPredicate
```

---

## 2. Supplementary Source: Circuit Breaker Design Document (Ml-engine & Firebolt)

**Source**: [Circuit Breaker: Ml-engine & Firebolt](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~185648802/pages/5684132441/Circuit+Breaker+Ml-engine+Firebolt)  
**Last Modified**: 2025-11-03  

### 2.1 Architecture Context
- **ML-Engine service** is the downstream service used for getting group-signatures for alerts
- When ML-Engine fails (5xx), it leads to **SQS retries (up to 10times)** before messages go to DLQ
- CB is applied at the **aiops-im-insights → aiops-ml-engine** call boundary
- Separate CBs can also protect **firebolt** calls

### 2.2 CB Scoping Strategy Chosen
Three approaches evaluated:
- **Global CB** (one for all traffic) — simple but noisy-neighbor risk
- **Region-based CB** (per region) — moderate isolation
- **Tenant-based CB** (per tenant) — full isolation but high memory/CPU overhead

The team confirmed CB config is **at downstream service level**, with each feature/service having different thresholds.

### 2.3 Rate Limit Integration
```
tenant → manual() → FF → ingestion → queue → requeue → main queue
Aiops-im-insights → rate limit + CB
Aiops-ml-engine → rate limit + handling (im-insights)
```

### 2.4 Release Plan (Switcheroo Gate)
- Feature gate: `aiops_circuit_breaker_enabled`
- Controlled via custom attributes: `environment` (starting from prod-west2hello tenant, then prod-east, etc.) and `service` attribute as `ML_ENGINE`
- Progressive rollout using Switcheroo/Statsig

### 2.5 Retry Behavior When CB is Open
When an event arrives while CB is open:
- The ml-engine call doesn't go through
- It throws an exception
- Message does NOT continue processing normally
- Message should go into a reprocessing queue (not retry10times)

