## 4. Incident Response Metrics (TTD/TTH/TTR/TTM/TTC)

**Sources**:
- [Operational Metrics in Time of Incident - Definitions](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/3036951819/Operational+Metrics+in+Time+of+Incident+-+Definitions)
- [PIR Changes Required to Support TTx Metrics](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Spork/pages/5893427416/PIR+Changes+Required+to+Support+TTx+Metrics+Ease+of+Use)
- [SEV Review Template](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/3023111932/SEV+Review+Template)

### 4.1 Metric Definitions (Atlassian-Official)

| Metric | Full Name | Calculation |
|--------|-----------|-------------|
| **TTD** | Time to Detect | Time from impact start to when the org is **aware** and has **acknowledged** the problem |
| **TTH** | Time to HOT | Time from Sev-2 breach to HOT creation (or HOT upgrade to Sev-2) |
| **TTM** | Time to Mitigate | Time from Sev-2 breach until Sev-2 impact is halted (no longer critical) |
| **TTR** | Time to Resolve | Time from detection to full resolution and service restoration |
| **TTC** | Time to Communicate | Time from HOT creation to first external communication |

### 4.2 SLO Targets at Atlassian

| Metric | Target |
|--------|--------|
| TTD | < 30 minutes (Detection from impact start) |
| TTH | < 25 minutes (HOT creation from major severity breach) |
| TTM | < 2 hours (Impact end from major severity breach) |
| TTC | < 30 minutes (From HOT Creation) |

### 4.3 PIR Metrics Table Template (for auto-generation)

```
| Metric Type | Result |
|-------------|--------|
| Detected by Monitoring? | Yes or No |
| TTD less than 30 minutes (Detection from impact start) | Yes or No |
| TTH less than 25 minutes (Hot creation from major severity breach) | Yes or No |
| TTM less than 2 hours (Impact end from major severity breach) | Yes or No |
| TTC less than 30 minutes (From Hot Creation) | Yes or No |
| Has this incident with similar root cause happened in the past12 months? | Yes or No |
| Root cause category field is filled and categorized accurately | Yes or No |
| Recovery by field is filled and categorized accurately | Yes or No |
| Preventable by field is filled and categorized accurately | Yes or No |
| Was progressive roll out and/or production change control followed? | Yes or No |
```

---

## 5. Incident Communication Cadence (Atlassian Standard)

**Sources**:
- [Send Internal Comms - go/sendcomms](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IMPIR/pages/3265766957/Send+Internal+Comms+-+go+sendcomms)
- [HOW TO: Send internal incident communications](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IMPIR/pages/3156352124/HOW+TO+Send+internal+incident+communications)
- [Atlassian Incident Handbook (approved)](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CHILL/pages/254784532/Atlassian+Incident+Handbook+approved)

### 5.1 Communication Timeline

| Phase | Timing | Content |
|-------|--------|---------|
| **First comms** | First 15-20 minutes | Light on info — focus on progress over perfection. Notify stakeholders that IC is actively managing. |
| **Second comms** | 50-60 minutes | Clear, concise. Sufficient info for stakeholders to understand impact and restoration state. |
| **Third and beyond** | Every 60minutes after previous | Steady cadence. Can be extended if status unchanged for long periods or waiting on blockers. |
| **Closing comms** | When incident resolved | State no further comms. Summarize incident, impact, response, resolution, follow-up actions. |

### 5.2 Internal Comms SLO
- **15-minute SLO** for initial internal communications (Sev-2+)
- **30-minute SLO** referenced frequently for initial comms in critical incidents
- Tool: `go/sendcomms` (sends internal email, updates internal Statuspage, HOT, and Slack channel)

### 5.3 Comms Six-Point Checklist
1. What is the actual impact on customers?
2. How many internal and external customers are affected?
3. If the root cause is known, what is it?
4. If there is an ETA for restoration, what is it?
5. When & where will the next update be?
6. Be explicit about unknowns

---

## 6. PIR Process and Timeline

**Sources**:
- [Incident Response Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/gir/pages/1540798526/Incident+Response+Plan)
- Various PIR pages

### 6.1 PIR Requirements by Severity

| Severity | PIR Required? |
|----------|--------------|
| Sev 0 | ✅ MANDATORY |
| Sev 1 | ✅ MANDATORY |
| Sev 2 | Optional (PIR-X light version available) |
| Sev 3 | Optional (PIR-X light version available) |

### 6.2 PIR SLA Timelines
- **Time to Draft Failure SLA**: 30 business days from creation
- **Time to Approval Failure SLA**: 14 business days from being sent for approval
