What exists (reusable):

 • Databricks SDK pattern (strong reuse) —
   model_onboarding/gpt-oss-safeguard-20b/05_pull_plato_hello_sample.py uses
   databricks.sdk.WorkspaceClient(profile=…) +
   statement_execution.execute_statement with the correct
   Disposition.EXTERNAL_LINKS + Format.JSON_ARRAY + per-link next_chunk_index
   pagination pattern. Covers auth (~/.databrickscfg profiles for plato-stg,
   plato-prod, ml-studio-stg/prod), SQL execution, polling state machine, and
   UC three-part-name table queries. Direct reuse for the Databricks+UC MCP
   tool.
 • Tarot v3 ML Registry wrapper —
   model_onboarding/gpt-oss-safeguard-20b/01_vllm-gpt-oss-safeguard-20b-it.py
   uses atlassian_msp_sdk.ml_registry (get_component,
   upload_artifact_with_data_labels, upload_artifact_folder_with_data_labels,
   create_version, annotations) and Launchpad (launch_to_teamserve). Covers
   the registry half of the MLflow+Tarot tool. Auth = runtime-bound ASAP
   principal (EXPERIMENTAL/ADHOC/RELEASED via atlas ml lab).
 • Skill authoring convention — .agents/skills/ai-employee-mle/ provides the
   {SKILL.md, bootstrap.md, manifest.json, references/*} template (with SHA256
   + change-history versioning) that new MCP-tool skill bundles should follow.

What is missing (must be built net-new):

 • ❌ Zero MLflow code — no mlflow imports anywhere; need MlflowClient wrapper
   for runs/params/metrics/registry/lineage and bit-exact replay (KPI 8.1).
 • ❌ Zero Tecton / MLFS code — no Feature Store SDK use; build from scratch
   on tecton SDK.
 • ❌ No MCP tool.json scaffolding in repo — follow external MCP-server
   convention.
 • ❌ SLAUTH module (src/slauth/user_context.py) is inbound-only (Flask header
   parser); not reusable for outbound auth. Use Databricks PAT/profile for
   MLflow + Databricks tools; ASAP for Tarot.
 • ❌ Databricks notebook submit, UC catalog/schema/table introspection,
   cluster lifecycle — must extend the existing SQL-only pattern.

Key gotchas to encode in tool design:

 • Disposition.INLINE 25 MB cap → default to EXTERNAL_LINKS.
 • result.next_chunk_index is always None — paginate via
   external_links[-1].next_chunk_index.
 • Tarot 403 from Databricks UI → re-launch via atlas ml lab or open SSAM
   permission with --asap "*".
 • databricks auth login requires browser SSO — bootstrap-only step, can't be
   headless.
 • Launchpad deploy ≈ 10–20 min — MCP tool timeouts must allow it.

Bit-exact MLflow replay approach: capture dataset digests + git SHA + uv
lockfile + Tarot artifact URI + deterministic env (PYTHONHASHSEED,
CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG, torch.use_deterministic_algorithms) at run-time;
replay re-resolves all of these and compares each metric with abs_tol=0. Audit
via SQL LEFT-JOIN of mlflow.runs against a replay_audit table.

Feature Store audit query design: the offline-side coverage/freshness/sparsity
audits can run as Databricks SQL on the UC offline materialization table
(reusing the existing SQL pattern) grouped by connector × region × tenant. The
online-side and consistency probe require the Tecton SDK (get_online_features,
get_historical_features, fv.summary()).


