Full report written to outputs/facet.md. Eight authoritative Confluence
sources fetched into artifacts/.

Key findings:


 1 No single REST admin API exists for AI Gateway routing. The control plane
   is a triplet: (a) atlas ml aigateway model {list,view,list --alias} CLI for
   the model registry, (b) Shipyard config + PRs for
   vendor_policy.{order,only}, model_overrides, tenant allowed_providers, and
   route configs in
   ai-gateway/src/main/kotlin/com/atlassian/aigateway/config/routes/, and (c)
   Statsig feature gates (deterministic cloudId bucketing) for runtime
   percentage control.
 2 Provider matrix: OpenAI (direct + on Bedrock + on TeamServe as GPT-OSS),
   Anthropic (Bedrock + Vertex + direct), Google/Gemini (Vertex primary),
   Amazon (Bedrock), and internal (TeamServe gRPC + MSP) via /v1/teamserve/*,
   /v1/msp/*, plus the unified POST /v2/responses Open-Responses route.
   models.yml (100+ models) carries provider:modelId + lifecycle stage
   (CRITICAL/ACTIVE/BETA/ALPHA/DEPRECATED).
 3 Canary primitive (canonical): Statsig "Gradual rollout framework" (M1.5) —
   percentage-based, cloudId-bucketed, per use-case × candidate-model.
   Sub-primitives: per-tenant pinning via ModelOverrideService, lifecycle
   stage promotion, and Chopper-PR route-priority changes for structural
   canaries.
 4 Shadow / mirror primitive (canonical): Statsig "shadow mode" gate that
   triggers non-blocking parallel dispatch on the AI Gateway (Netty
   event-loop, BlockHound-enforced). Responses are logged/metricized but not
   streamed to caller. Cost-doubling and first-byte-only constraints are
   explicit limitations. Cross-model comparison harness is an explicit
   Non-Goal of the SLO Router — it's the integration seam for the
   Eval-framework tool (1C).
 5 Policy waterfall (tenant → session-pin → SLO/use-case → default tiering) —
   tenant is the only hard constraint; session and SLO are soft and
   overridable. M2 introduces VendorFallbackFilter (retryable: 429, 5xx,
   timeout; non-retryable: 400/401/403/404/413).
 6 Recommended tool surface (12 ops) mapped with Symphony 🟢/🟡/🔴 tiers,
   including list_models, view_model, probe_routing (debug headers
   X-Atlassian-Serving-*), set_canary, pin_tenant, enable_shadow (emits
   eval-job handle), set_fallback_strategy
   (DEFAULT/ENFORCED/LLAMA_70B/GPT_OSS_*/NONE), register_model (🔴 multi-repo
   PR + slauth POST /api/ai-gateway/model), and submit_chopper_checklist.
 7 Critical footguns to encode: empty-vendor-list collapse from
   vendor_policy.only, cross-provider reasoning-token corruption in multi-turn
   (Claude/Gemini-3) until M3 ships gateway-side stripping,
   eventual-consistency on policy writes, and cost spike from shadow traffic.
 8 Integration with sibling tools: shadow mode hands off to Eval-framework 
   tool (1C) for offline quality comparison; chopper-checklist drafting uses
   Atlassian MCP (create_confluence_page); Statsig writes use Switcheroo MCP
   (switcheroo_create_gate); register-model PR drafting uses Bitbucket MCP (no
   overlap with Bitbucket Pipelines per constraint 1B).
