## 3. Deployment Manifest

### What It Is
A structured document that captures all information needed to deploy, verify, rollback, and monitor an ML model in production. It serves as both a pre-deployment checklist and a living record of deployment state.

### Internal Template: ML Launch Review Checklist

**Source:** [[Template] ML Launch Review Checklist](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/4818634684/Template+ML+Launch+Review+Checklist)

This is the canonical Atlassian internal template with two phases:

**Phase 1: Pre-Experiment**
| Phase | Process | Checklist | Priority |
|-------|---------|-----------|----------|
| General | Planning and scoping | Project Poster | Must Have |
| General | ML solution design | Design documentation | Must Have |
| General | Experiment Pre-analysis | Pre-analysis notebook | Must Have |
| Model Validation | Model validation/analysis | Face/internal/external validation, Feature importance | Must Have |
| Data/Feature Engineering | Production data pipeline | Feature engineering pipeline (code reviewed, checked in) | Must Have |
| Model Development | Training pipeline | Model training pipeline (code reviewed) | Must Have |
| Model Development | Offline evaluation | Offline evaluation notebook | Must Have |
| Model Development | Register model | Model registry with version control | Must Have |
| Model Deployment | Inference pipeline | Generates expected output schema + unit tests | Must Have |
| Model Deployment | Integration test | Integration with GRS/GUPS/etc | Must Have |
| Model Deployment | Edge cases | Default recommendation if no score | Must Have |
| Experiment Setup | Experiment templates | From Galileo team | Must Have |

**Phase 2: Pre-Production**
| Phase | Process | Checklist | Priority |
|-------|---------|-----------|----------|
| General | Privacy & Compliance | Privacy and security review | Must Have |
| General | Experiment Post-analysis | Post-analysis notebook | Must Have |
| Model Development | Retraining pipeline | Model auto-retraining pipeline | Must Have |
| Model Deployment | Rollback plan | Model roll-back plan | Must Have |
| Model Deployment | Latency Analysis | Serving pipeline latency analysis | Must Have |
| Monitoring | Data quality | Data/feature drifting monitor | Must Have |
| Monitoring | Model inference | Model inference metrics monitor | Must Have |
| Monitoring | Infra health | Infra health monitor (latency) | Must Have |
| Monitoring | Alerts | Opsgenie/alerts to Slack | Must Have |

### TEAMServe Deployment Workflow

From [How To: Deploy ML Models to TEAMServe](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120204aa07fe7450f489899b60900ad6a0967/pages/5959589965):

```
0. Prerequisites
   - Fill deployment template
   - Plan compute capacity (GPU estimation per region)
   - Engage backend team for code integration
   - Check compliance

1. Model Development & Packaging
   Exit: Package builds + available in AI model registry

2. Unit Test
   Exit: Logic correct + latency within KR + inference API correct
   How: Launchpad

3. Validate TEAMServe Setup
   Exit: Artifact deployed to endpoint + endpoint running + health check passes + auth configured
   How: QD, scraper

4. Validate Integration
   Exit: Scores as expected + latency within KR
   How: Scraper, autoscraper, perfhammer

5. Experimentation
   - Capacity available
   - Pause if SLO breach
   How: Monitor metrics

6. Triage & Production Launch
   - Pre-launch checklist filled
   - Production capacity available
```

### Model Owner Deployment Checklist

From [Model Owner Guides](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020a570c71e24c846068af97060212d4544/pages/6894978116):
```
- [ ] Model shows as compliant
- [ ] Model packaged as triton module in ml-studio
- [ ] Required files: config.pbtxt, model.py, model.pt, config.json, tokenizer/autopackage.py
- [ ] Launchpad validation: config.pbtxt validated locally, unit tests passed
- [ ] Model registered in ML registry (not manual upload)
- [ ] ML Registry componentRef /VersionRef confirmed
- [ ] Unique Subfolder Naming
