## 4. Architecture Comparison Report

### What It Is
A structured comparison of multiple model architectures evaluated for the same task, capturing trade-offs across performance, latency, cost, complexity, and maintainability. Supports the SOP-2 workflow requirement of "5-10 parallel architectures → mandatory ablation → exhaustive error analysis → decision."

### Internal Patterns Found

**Pattern 1: Evaluation Framework Comparison Matrix** (from [SPIKE: ML Evaluation Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202036af61f960604897b3e8da6cda3794c0/pages/6098222361))

```
| Requirement | Option A | Option B | Winner |
|-------------|----------|----------|--------|
| Integration | Excellent | Good | A |
| Automation | Very Good | Very Good | Tie |
| Flexibility | Limited | Excellent | B |
| Ease of Use | Excellent | Good | A |
| Data Access | Limited | Excellent | B |
```

**Pattern 2: Architecture Design Comparison** (from DevBluePrint M3/M5 pattern):
- Each option includes: Component selection with justification
- Maps requirements to components
- Estimates cost and complexity
- States assumptions and risks
- Compares alternatives with trade-off analysis

**Pattern 3: ML Model Comparison** (from [Authorization Vulnerability Scoring](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/JALN/pages/6411309538)):
```
| Model | Training Accuracy | CV Accuracy |
|-------|-------------------|-------------|
| LR (C=0.5) | 68.9% | 64.7% |
| RF (depth=6) | 79.5% | 59.5% |
```

**Pattern 4: GKE Cost/Performance Analysis** (from [Evolving ML Fabric](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6364624214)):
- H200 costs on AWS vs GCP
- Node cold-start times
- Operational characteristics comparison

