## Cross-Cutting Patterns & Autonomy Classification

### Symphony3-Tier Autonomy Mapping for Templates

| Template | Generate | Review | Publish |
|----------|----------|--------|---------|
| Model Card | 🟢 Auto-populate metadata | 🟡 Human reviews ethical/limitations | 🟡 Human approves |
| Experiment Report | 🟢 Auto-populate metrics/results | 🟡 Human reviews hypothesis/decision | 🟢 Auto-publish after approval |
| Deployment Manifest | 🟢 Auto-populate from registry | 🔴 Human must confirm compliance | 🔴 Human approves deployment |
| Architecture Comparison | 🟢 Auto-generate comparison matrix | 🟡 Human reviews recommendation | 🟢 Auto-publish |
| Weekly Digest | 🟢 Fully auto-generated | 🟢 Optional review | 🟢 Auto-publish + Slack |

### Common MCP Operations Across All Templates

| MCP Toolset | Used By Templates |
|-------------|-------------------|
| `atlassian/confluence` (create_page, update_page, search_cql) | All 5 |
| `atlassian/jira` (create_issue, update_issue, search_jql) | Experiment Report, Deployment Manifest, Weekly Digest |
| `eval-framework` (new) | Model Card, Experiment Report, Architecture Comparison, Weekly Digest |
| `ML CI/CD` (new) | All 5 |
| `serving-infra` (new) | Deployment Manifest, Weekly Digest |
| `slack` (send_message) | Weekly Digest, Deployment Manifest (alerts) |
| `bitbucket` (repo content) | Deployment Manifest (config files) |
| `compass` (component links) | Deployment Manifest |

### Template Versioning & Evolution

All templates should be stored as Confluence page templates with:
- Version history tracked via page versions
- Template variables for auto-population
- Clear section markers for agent vs. human authorship
- Inline validation rules (e.g., "this section must contain at least 5 error examples")

