─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Key findings:

  1 No local Spinnaker tooling exists — only twg skill present;
    bitbucketPipeline MCP covers Bitbucket Pipelines (must not be duplicated).
    This is greenfield.
  2 Gate API surface (Atlassian deployment):
     • Hosts: spinnaker-dev-gate.internal.shared-dev.us-west-2.kitt-inf.net
       (dev), spinnaker-prod.internal.shared-prod.us-east-1.kitt-inf.net
       (prod). Separate gates per env.
     • Auth: atlas slauth curl --aud spinnaker -- ... (users), atlas micros 
       service deploytoken add (services).
     • Swagger at /swagger-ui.html; OSS reference at
       spinnaker.io/docs/reference/api/docs.
  3 Trigger (canonical): POST 
    {GATE}/pipelines/{application}/{pipelineNameOrId}
    (invokePipelineConfigUsingPOST1). Body is the trigger (no wrapper).
    Returns 202. Minimal viable trigger needs type=manual,
    artifacts[].metadata.source (config-registry pointer + namespace + tag).
    Alternatives /applications/.../pipelineConfigs/{name} and /pipelines/start
    exist but inferior.
  4 Listing & status:
     • List configs: GET /applications/{app}/pipelineConfigs.
     • Recent executions: GET 
       /applications/{app}/pipelines?limit=N&expand=true&statuses=....
     • Single execution (with stages + outputs): GET /pipelines/{executionId}.
       No separate stage-output or log endpoint — walk
       stages[i].context/outputs/tasks/exception and recurse into child
       executionIds.
     • Control: PUT /pipelines/{id}/cancel|pause|resume, PUT 
       /pipelines/{id}/stages/{stageId}/restart.
  5 Execution-ID discovery problem (Atlassian-specific): Gate trigger response
    has no executionId. Resolve via (a) SLS GET 
    /api/v1/execution/{slsExecutionId}/minimal —
    stepOutput.additionalDetails.executionIds[]; (b) Wrangler
    /api/v1/archetype/.../executions (flaky); or (c) caller-minted eventId
    polled against GET /applications/{app}/pipelines.
  6 Integration boundaries: Bitbucket MCP owns build/step/log for Bitbucket
    Pipelines; new Spinnaker tool owns Gate. Boundary helper
    spin_link_bitbucket_build connects "Upload Spinnaker Custom Pipelines"
    stage output → Spinnaker execution. Config Registry
    (config-registry.prod.atl-paas.net) supplies artifact metadata for trigger
    construction. Micros service-descriptor write should be
    plan-only/PR-based, not autonomous.
  7 Recommended autonomy split: read-only ops (list/get) auto; trigger +
    pause/resume auto-with-audit; cancel/restart/POST-tasks/POST-pipelines
    confirmation-gated.
  8 Edge cases: stale RUNNING executions common; deterministic UUIDs preferred
    over names; SSAM membership required for prod; {"trigger": {...}} wrappers
    silently ignored; gate returns 400 with JSON error/message/status/traceId;
    validation errors often surface only in the Micros Deploy stage
    post-trigger.
  9 Suggested tool primitives: spin_pipelines_list,
    spin_service_descriptor_get, spin_pipeline_trigger,
    spin_execution_resolve(eventId),
    spin_execution_get(include_children=true),
    spin_execution_cancel/restart_stage (gated), spin_link_bitbucket_build.


