## 3. Autonomy Thresholds (🟢/🟡/🔴) for SOP-1

### 3.1 Symphony3-Tier Autonomy Model (Authoritative Definition)

From the Atlassian Symphony AI Employee Orchestration Platform document:

| **Tier** | **Signal** | **Meaning** | **Criteria** |
|---|---|---|---|
| **1 — Autonomous** | 🟢 | Agent acts without human approval | Known pattern, within policy scope, bounded blast radius |
| **2 — Confirm** | 🟡 | Agent proposes action with reasoning; human approves with single click | Novel patterns or higher-stakes decisions |
| **3 — Escalate** | 🔴 | Agent hits hard policy boundary; pages human with full context | Human makes the call |

**Key principles**:
- Policies are version-controlled, auditable, and human-authored
- The AI employee proposes policy updates when it identifies gaps — humans approve all changes
- Autonomy is bounded by what humans have explicitly permitted; it never exceeds it

**Source**: [Atlassian Symphony: AI Employee Orchestration Platform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6933824809)

### 3.2 Digital MLE Autonomy Mapping (Direct Precedent for SOP-1)

From the Digital MLE: AI Employee Vision document — the authoritative mapping for ML retraining autonomy:

| **Activity in Retraining Workflow** | **Autonomy** | **Justification** |
|---|---|---|
| Monitoring signal freshness against SLA | 🟢 Autonomous | Bounded blast radius — read-only observation |
| Detecting feature drift and training/serving skew | 🟢 Autonomous | Monitoring and alerting only |
| Auto-triggering data refresh workflows within policy | 🟢 Autonomous | Known pattern, within policy scope |
| Scheduled retraining runs within defined cadence | 🟢 Autonomous | Known pattern, bounded blast radius |
| Generating training run summaries | 🟢 Autonomous | Read-only reporting |
| Comparing model versions on offline metrics | 🟢 Autonomous | No production impact |
| Flagging when model age exceeds refresh policy | 🟢 Autonomous | Alerting only |
| New signal/data source ingestion | 🟡 Confirm | Novel pattern — new scope |
| Architecture changes during retraining | 🟡 Confirm | Higher-stakes decision |
| Regression interpretation | 🟡 Confirm | Requires domain judgment |
| Cross-team data agreements | 🔴 Escalate | Hard policy boundary |
| Model design decisions | 🔴 Escalate | Fundamental research judgment |
| Launch/rollback recommendation | 🔴 Escalate | Production impact decision |
| Model deployment to production | 🔴 Escalate | Explicit RFC decision: deployment remains manual |

**Source**: [Digital MLE: AI Employee Vision](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/7051610727)

### 3.3 SOP-1 Step-by-Step Autonomy Classification

Synthesizing from the Digital MLE Vision, Symphony framework, and the ML Pipeline CI/CD Framework, here is the proposed9-step SOP-1 with autonomy tier assignments:

| **Step** | **Action** | **Autonomy** | **Rationale** |
|---|---|---|---|
| **1. Detect Drift** | Run drift detection metrics (PSI, KS, etc.) against reference window | 🟢 | Read-only computation, no side effects |
| **2. Evaluate Severity** | Compare drift values against configured thresholds; classify as warning/error | 🟢 | Rule-based evaluation, bounded |
| **3. Correlate with Output** | Check if input drift correlates with output/prediction drift | 🟢 | Additional monitoring step, read-only |
| **4. Assess Retraining Need** | Apply decision matrix (input drift × output drift → action) | 🟢 if within known patterns; 🟡 if novel pattern | Depends on whether drift pattern has been seen before |
| **5. Prepare Training Data** | Refresh data pipeline, apply tenant filters, validate quality | 🟢 | Within policy scope, standard pipeline run |
| **6. Execute Retraining** | Submit training job via ML Studio Orchestrator | 🟢 for scheduled/cadence; 🟡 for drift-triggered | Drift-triggered is a slightly novel trigger vs. pure schedule |
| **7. Validate Model Quality** | Run offline eval, compare metrics against quality gates | 🟢 | No production impact; read-only eval |
| **8. Register Model** | Version and tag model in ML Registry | 🟡 | Writes to production artifact store; confirm version |
| **9. Promote to Production** | Deploy retrained model to serving | 🔴 | Production impact; human makes launch decision |

**Source**: Synthesized from [Digital MLE Vision](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/7051610727), [ML Pipeline CI/CD Validation Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~6359788e1cc605b1fd1664ec/pages/6723101866), [RFC: Model Re-training](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6013257858)

### 3.4 Threshold-Based Tier Determination Logic

For encoding in SKILL.md, the drift signal → autonomy tier mapping:

```
IF drift_detected:IF PSI < 0.1 AND all quality checks pass:
    → 🟢 No action needed. Log and continue monitoring.
  
  IF 0.1 ≤ PSI < 0.25 OR quality_check_warning:
    → 🟢 Autonomous: Increase monitoring frequency (daily → 4x/day)
    → 🟢 Autonomous: Generate drift report and post to Slack
    → 🟡 Confirm: If model age > refresh_window, propose retraining
  
  IF PSI ≥ 0.25 OR quality_check_error:
    → 🟢 Autonomous: Generate detailed drift analysis
    → 🟢 Autonomous: Prepare training data pipeline
    → 🟡 Confirm: Propose retraining with reasoning to human
    → Wait for human approval (single-click confirm)
    → 🟢 Autonomous: Execute retraining (post-approval)
    → 🟢 Autonomous: Run offline eval
    → 🟡 Confirm: Present eval results and propose registration
    → 🔴 Escalate: Deployment to production (human decides)
  
  IF PSI > 0.5 OR multiple features in error simultaneously:
    → 🔴 Escalate: Page human with full context
    → Investigation required before any automated action
    → Possible data pipeline failure (not model issue)
```

### 3.5 Safety Constraints (Non-Negotiables)

From the hire_a_tpm kit precedent and Symphony documentation:

1. **Never deploy to production autonomously** — this is a hard 🔴 stop across all AI employee roles
2. **Never modify training data sources autonomously** — cross-team data agreement changes require 🔴
3. **All write operations produce audit trails** — Confluence page, Jira ticket, Slack thread, decision log
4. **Model rollback is always🔴** — human makes the call
5. **Policy scope changes require human approval** — if drift pattern is novel (not previously seen), escalate to🟡

