## 5. ERROR-ANALYSIS FRAMEWORKS

### 5.1 What It Is
A systematic methodology for categorizing, quantifying, and prioritizing model failures to guide improvement iterations.

### 5.2 How It Works — Internal Patterns

**Failure Categorization Framework** (from [Failure Categorization and Root Cause Analytics](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/fde/pages/6990288386)):

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  FAILURE DISTRIBUTION — [Model Name] (Last 30 Days)         │
│                                                              │
│  ████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░  Knowledge Gap42%       │
│  ██████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  Prompt Issue     28%       │
│  ████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  Context Loss     16%       │
│  ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░Edge Case9%       │
│  ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  Scoring Error     5%       │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Two-Pass Classification Pattern:**
- **Pass 1: Automated** — cheap checks (length, truncation, JSON.parse), regex/structural checks, then "other"
- **Pass 2: SME Review** — route to human when LLM confidence < 0.7, or category = unclear

**Offline Snippet Parse Failures Playbook** (from [Offline/online snippet parse failures](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121d50f9c1c478e4c7bb24be9eb9a3ea485/pages/6733344716)):

Fixed taxonomy BEFORE analyzing:
| Category | Typical Signal |
|----------|---------------|
| Empty/null response | No text or whitespace only |
| Truncation | Response cuts off mid-JSON |
| Wrong wrapper | Prose instead of expected structure |
| Malformed JSON | JSON.parse fails |
| Schema mismatch | Valid JSON but missing required keys |
| Regex/extractor miss | Structure present but extraction fails |
| Semantic garbage | Parse succeeds but content is nonsense |
| Tool/API error masked | Error message returned as normal completion |

**CI Failure Classification3-Tier Pattern** (from [Automating CI/CD Failure Analysis](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/coreengdc/pages/6428397133)):
```
Log → REGEX → ML → LLM → Classification↓       ↓    ↓40%    57%   3%
```
- Tier 1: Deterministic (regex) — instant, high confidence
- Tier 2: ML classifier — handles complex patterns
- Tier 3: LLM — semantic reasoning for novel errors

### 5.3 Exhaustive Error Analysis Workflow for ML Experiments

```
Step 1: Define Error Taxonomy (BEFORE looking at results)
  - Define mutually exclusive categories
  - Categories should be: [Model Error | Data Error | Label Error | Edge Case | OOD | Annotation Disagreement]
  - For ranking/retrieval: [False Positive | False Negative | Rank Swap | Missing from Corpus | Query Mismatch]

Step 2: Sample and Classify
  - Random sample of failures (minimum 100 for statistical validity)
  - Stratify by: error severity, data cohort, query type
  - Apply 2-pass classification (automated + human review on ambiguous)

Step 3: Quantify Distribution
  - Distribution chart (Pareto: 80/20 rule — which categories account for most failures)
  - Per-cohort breakdown (which user segments are most affected)
  - Trend over experiment iterations (are we making progress on specific categories)

Step 4: Root Cause Deep Dive (top 2-3 categories)
  - For each top category: examine 10+ exemplars
  - Identify patterns: data quality, feature gaps, architectural limitations
  - Map to actionable remediation: more data, different features, architecture change, label fix

Step 5: Prioritize Remediation
  - Impact × Fixability matrix
  - Generate next experiment hypothesis from error analysis findings
```

### 5.4 How It Applies to SKILL.md

The AI employee should:
- **🟢 Autonomous**: Define error taxonomy from eval results, classify failures automatically (pass 1)
- **🟢 Autonomous**: Generate distribution charts, per-cohort breakdowns, Pareto analysis
- **🟡 Confirm**: Present top failure categories with exemplars for human review (pass 2)
- **🟡 Confirm**: Propose remediation priorities and next experiment hypothesis
- **🔴 Human required**: Approve remediation strategy and resource allocation

**Source:** [Failure Categorization and Root Cause Analytics](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/fde/pages/6990288386), [Offline/online snippet parse failures playbook](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121d50f9c1c478e4c7bb24be9eb9a3ea485/pages/6733344716), [Automating CI/CD Failure Analysis](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/coreengdc/pages/6428397133), [AI Quality Improvement Framework from AIX](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AM3/pages/4157214981)

