## 6. DECISION CRITERIA

### 6.1 What It Is
A framework for making go/no-go decisions on whether to ship a model variant, iterate further, or abandon an approach — combining statistical significance, practical significance, and operational readiness.

### 6.2 How It Works — Internal Patterns

**Statistical vs. Practical Significance** (from [Coursework - Reading Experiment Results in Statsig](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~754555057/pages/6859438980)):

| Concept | Definition | Threshold |
|---------|-----------|-----------|
| Statistical significance | Effect unlikely due to chance | p < 0.05, CI doesn't cross zero |
| Practical significance | Effect large enough to be worth acting on | Lift ≥ MDE (Minimum Detectable Effect) |
| Guardrail metrics | Must not regress | All green required to ship |

**Decision Matrix Pattern** (from [Edit with TTS - Launch Data Evaluation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/loomhq/pages/5405522172)):

| Decision | Criteria |
|----------|---------|
|🚨 Halt & Investigate | Any guardrail metric drops > threshold, error rate > 5% |
|⚖️ Maintain & Monitor | Adoption below target but no regressions |
| ✅ Ship/GA | All guardrails green + primary metric exceeds MDE |

**A/B Test Experiment Runbook Decision Flow** (from [AIX - AB Test Experiment Runbook](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AM3/pages/5893600845)):

```
Step 1: Sufficient reason to proceed?
  IF offline lift in primary metric AND supporting metrics pass → proceed
  IF no offline eval possible → adequate rationale + stakeholder review

Step 1b: Side-by-side comparisons
  - Representative sample of test data
  - Human reviewers label which response is better
  - Calculate preference metrics

Step 2: Design experiment plan
  - Define hypothesis
  - Set MDE expectation
  - Design traffic allocation
  - Finalize primary + supporting + guardrail metrics
  - Check metrics availability

Step 3: Execute and analyze
  - Wait for sufficient sample size
  - Check statistical significance
  - Check practical significance
  - Verify guardrails
```

**Growth Experiment Lifecycle Decision Points** (from [Experiment Lifecycle Phases](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Growth/pages/5314320858)):
```
POST ANALYSIS → Decision from Weekly Experiment Review →SHIPPED-CONTROL (unsuccessful) OR
  SHIPPED-VARIATION (success or no-harm) →
  PRODUCTIONISING → PRODUCTIONISED
```

### 6.3 ML Experiment Decision Framework (Synthesized)

```markdown
## Decision Criteria for Experiment [NAME]

### Pre-conditions (must ALL be true to consider shipping)
- [ ] Statistical significance: p < 0.05 on primary metric
- [ ] Confidence interval does NOT cross zero
- [ ] Sufficient sample size reached (per pre-analysis power calculation)
- [ ] All guardrail metrics within acceptable bounds

### Primary Decision
| Outcome | Action | Criteria |
|---------|--------|---------|
| **Clear Win** | Ship | Primary metric ≥ MDE, all guardrails green, ablation confirms no unnecessary complexity |
| **Marginal Win** | Iterate | Primary metric positive but< MDE, OR one guardrail amber |
| **No Effect** | Abandon approach | CI crosses zero after sufficient sample, OR MDE unreachable |
| **Regression** | Halt immediately | Primary metric negative OR any guardrail red |

### Additional ML-Specific Decision Factors
| Factor | Ship Threshold | Iterate Threshold | Abandon Threshold |
|--------|---------------|-------------------|-------------------|
| Offline metric lift | ≥ pre-defined MDE | >0but < MDE |≤ 0 |
| Latency impact (P90) | < 5% regression | 5-15% regression | > 15% regression |
| Cost per inference | ≤ budget | 1-2x budget | > 2x budget |
| Error analysis coverage | Top category addressable | Top category partially understood | Top category intractable |
| Ablation confirms value | All components justified | Some components redundant | Architecture fundamentally wrong |

### Negative Result Documentation (MANDATORY)
Even if experiment is abandoned:
- What was tried
- Why it didn't work (with evidence)
- What was learned
- Recommendation for what NOT to try next
```

### 6.4 How It Applies to SKILL.md

The AI employee should:
- **🟢 Autonomous**: Compute statistical significance, CI, effect sizes
- **🟢 Autonomous**: Check all guardrail metrics against thresholds
- **🟢 Autonomous**: Generate decision recommendation with evidence table
- **🟡 Confirm**: Present decision recommendation to human for approval
- **🔴 Human required**: Final go/no-go decision, especially for production deployment

**Source:** [AIX - AB Test Experiment Runbook](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AM3/pages/5893600845), [Coursework - Reading Experiment Results in Statsig](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~754555057/pages/6859438980), [Experiment Lifecycle Phases](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Growth/pages/5314320858), [Edit with TTS - Launch Data Evaluation Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/loomhq/pages/5405522172)

