## 10. KEY TERMINOLOGY THE AI EMPLOYEE MUST UNDERSTAND

| Term | Definition |
|------|-----------|
| **MDE** | Minimum Detectable Effect — smallest meaningful improvement worth shipping |
| **Guardrail metric** | Metric that must NOT regress (latency, error rate, cost) |
| **Ablation** | Removing one component to measure its contribution |
| **Marginal lift** | Performance gain attributable to a single component |
| **Layer Attribution Matrix** | Table mapping each system component to its contribution per metric |
| **Kill criteria** | Pre-defined conditions under which to abandon an experiment |
| **N≥3** | Minimum replications required for variance estimation |
| **p-value** | Probability of observing result under null hypothesis |
| **Confidence interval** | Range likely containing true effect |
| **MRR@K / NDCG@K** | Primary ranking metrics used at Atlassian |
| **ML Studio** | Atlassian's internal training platform (Databricks-based) |
| **mlexp** | Internal CLI for experiment tracking |
| **ML Lens** | Internal model monitoring system |
| **Negative result** | Experiment that didn't achieve its hypothesis — MUST be documented |

