## 1. HYPOTHESIS FRAMING

### 1.1 What It Is
A structured method for stating testable ML experiment hypotheses that clearly define the causal relationship, directionality, measurable variables, and falsifiability criteria.

### 1.2 How It Works — Atlassian-Internal Template

From internal Experimentation Best Practices ([Hypothesis-driven design](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/band/pages/3666042907/Hypothesis-driven+design+-+what+why+and+how)):

**Template:**
```
We believe that: [assumption/change] will lead to: [measurable outcome]
We will test this by doing: [plan/experiment design]
We expect to see: [quantitative threshold/expected result]
```

**Rules (from internal docs):**
1. States a causal relationship with a clear actor
2. Has directionality (increase/decrease)
3. States variables that can be manipulated AND measured
4. Is testable with an experiment
5. Is a falsifiable statement

**Growth Engineering Framework extension** (from [Experiment Design Template](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Growth/pages/3110851265/Experiment+Design+JPD-ID)):
```
Hypothesis:IF [we make this specific change]
  THEN [this metric will improve by X%]
  BECAUSE [mechanism/rationale]
  We will succeed if: we see a [Y]% uplift in [primary metric]
```

### 1.3 ML-Specific Hypothesis Framing (Synthesized from Multiple Sources)

For ML experiments, the hypothesis must additionally specify:

| Field | Description | Example |
|-------|-------------|---------|
| **Assumption** | What you believe about the model/data | "Adding behavioral features improves relevance for tenants with >1K issues" |
| **Independent Variable** | What you're changing | Model architecture, hyperparameter, feature set, data preprocessing |
| **Dependent Variable** | What you're measuring | MRR@10, NDCG@10, latency P90, inference cost |
| **Control** | Baseline comparison | Current production model / previous best experiment |
| **Mechanism** | Why you believe this will work | "Behavioral signals capture user intent not represented in content features" |
| **Kill criteria** | When to abandon | "If offline metrics regress >2% on any guardrail metric" |
| **Expected magnitude** | How much improvement | "+5% MRR@10 relative lift" |

### 1.4 How It Applies to SKILL.md

The AI employee should:
- **🟢 Autonomous**: Auto-generate hypothesis template with placeholders filled from prior experiment context
- **🟡 Confirm**: Validate hypothesis completeness (all fields present) and flag missing kill criteria
- **🔴 Human required**: Approve the hypothesis statement and expected magnitude before experiment execution begins

**Source:** [Experimentation Best Practices - Hypothesis Driven - Impact Phase1 - J-LOVE](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/JLKB/pages/1880472371), [Hypothesis-driven design](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/band/pages/3666042907), [Experiment Design Template](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Growth/pages/3110851265), [ML-driven MFY Experiment Phase Checklist](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Spork/pages/6157225057)

