Scope & local context. Workspace contains no responsible-ai-api source — only
HTML spinner pages. Pulled scope from the parent breakdown (AI MLE role,
Subtask 1: ML Platform Tools Bundle). Report therefore documents the public 
MLflow Python SDK surface (which is what Atlassian's Databricks-hosted MLflow
exposes) and flags internal Atlassian artifacts (Tarot v3 tag schema, Slauth
precedence, etc.) as gaps the implementer must reconcile.

MlflowClient surface decomposed into 5 groups with full method tables
(inputs/outputs/notes):

 1 Experiments (search/create/get/rename/delete/tag)
 2 Runs (create/get/search/update/terminate/delete + tag CRUD)
 3 Params, metrics, tags, artifacts, inputs (log + read; log_batch caps;
   get_metric_history paging)
 4 Model Registry under Unity Catalog (Tarot v3): emphasizes aliases
   (@champion/@prod) over deprecated stages; 3-level names; copy_model_version
   for cross-catalog promotion
 5 Lineage via mlflow.data.Dataset.digest + log_inputs + UC
   system.lineage.table_lineage cross-checks

Capability matrix of ~18 wrapper commands with required/optional inputs,
output schemas, auth scopes, and backing API calls — stateless MlflowClient
(no fluent API) for safe concurrent agent use.

Bit-exact metric replay design (KPI 8.1):

 • Defined Canonical Replay Equality ≡_R — params strictly equal; metric
   histories canonicalized by (step, IEEE-754 hex repr of value) with
   timestamps dropped; dataset digests + artifact sha256 equal; NaN normalized
 • 6-phase replay algorithm: capture manifest → reconstruct env (git checkout
   + pip-sync from env_lock tag) → re-execute entrypoint in new run tagged
   replay::<orig_id> → recapture → diff → persist replay/report.json
 • Required tag contract on original runs: git_commit,
   mlflow.project.entryPoint, env_lock, random_seed.*, hardware.gpu_model,
   hardware.cuda_version, tecton.fv.snapshot_id, unity_catalog.table_versions
 • Diagnostic table mapping each divergence class (param drift, dataset
   digest, GPU non-determinism, serializer drift) to root cause + remediation
 • Throughput notes: 1000-metric log_batch cap, ~80 req/s throttle, 25k-point
   page size on get_metric_history, parallel per-key fetch

Integration patterns for SOP-1 retraining, SOP-2 experiment cycle, SOP-3
incident PIR, weekly digest, and day-one reproducibility audit.

AI-autonomy classification of every operation (🟢 reads + owned-run writes +
replay; 🟡 cross-governance writes; 🔴 alias-to-prod + destructive).


Gaps delegated to sibling workers: responsible-ai-api packaging conventions,
Slauth/PAT discriminator, Tarot v3 tag schema, UC privilege bootstrap,
per-framework determinism toolkit.
