### 2.4 TEAMServe & SageMaker Cost Optimization Plan

**What it is**: A structured cost reduction execution plan addressing both TEAMServe overprovisioning and SageMaker deprecation.

**How it works** (from TEAMServe & SageMaker Cost Optimization Plan H1FY2026):

**TEAMServe ($16M projected FY2026)**:
- Remove redundant/overprovisioned nodes
- Remove redundant reservations
- Migrate endpoints from services to TEAMServe
- Model packing (3x cost reduction demonstrated — multiple models sharing one GPU)
- Experiment packing: co-deploy experiments alongside production models

**SageMaker ($22k-30k/day)**:
- Idle endpoint reduction (reduced from ~$8500to $3800idle capacity)
- TEAMServe migration task force for remaining active endpoints
- Better forecast for savings plan renewal
- Identified ~$4k of remaining idle instances to remove

**How it applies**: The skill should:
- Maintain running inventory of active SageMaker and TEAMServe endpoints
- Calculate per-endpoint monthly burn rate
- Flag idle endpoints (no traffic for >7 days)
- Recommend model packing opportunities based on VRAM headroom and traffic patterns
- Track savings plan utilization and renewal timing

**Source**: [TEAMServe & SageMaker Cost Optimization Plan H1FY2026](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020ff70b14e5dca488b8ea018f735980b62/pages/5982146547)

