## 5. Industry Best Practices Context

### 5.1 FinOps Foundation FOCUS Standard
- Atlassian adopted FOCUS (FinOps Cost and Usage Specification) in October 2025
- Normalizes cost data across AWS, GCP, Azure, Databricks, Splunk
- Enables vendor-agnostic cost reporting through a unified schema
- The skill should output cost data in FOCUS-aligned categories

### 5.2 Unit Economics Framework
- Atlassian is building "Cost Per Unit" as a standard cultural change
- Metrics include: cost per active user, cost per API call, cost per search query, cost per inference request
- The skill should calculate and track unit costs for ML workloads (cost per model inference, cost per training epoch)

### 5.3 FCop (FinOps Cost Optimization) Platform
- Automated recommendation engine for instance selection and rightsizing
- Leverages AWS Cost Optimizer + internal observability data
- Starting with EC2, extending to GPU instances
- The skill should integrate with FCop recommendations when available

### 5.4 ML Studio FinOps Vision (May 2026)
- **Phase 1: Attribution** — Improve cost visibility per use case
- **Phase 2: Proactive Detection** — Anomaly alerts on data transfer, threshold/trend alerts for high-risk workflows
- **Phase 3: Optimization Experimentation Framework** — "Cost Optimisation Sandbox" for testing changes in isolated environments with before/after metrics

**Source**: [ML Studio and FinOps Cost Optimization Vision](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CFINOPS/pages/6822234480)

