(5924157618), ML Studio One‑Pager (3236010671), ML Registry user guide / Tarot
v3 (4594240174 + 6782624039 + 4836534532), ML Databricks (5796075518), MLflow
Integration in Airlock Flows (6659921772), FeatureView (MLFS) (6100075359),
Tecton Practical Guide (936191989), Tecton→MLFS Migration Status (6685373747),
Batch FV Migration Toolkit (6440579874), Unity Catalog Migration / View UC 
Grants RUNBOOK (2359990668 / 6311521526), CoreML MLOps Enhancement Plan
(6485707740).

2. Auth / endpoints verified.

 • MLflow tracking: databricks://socrates-public:ml-databricks →
   https://atlassian-ml-platform.cloud.databricks.com; OBO token minted by
   ml_fabric_create_run, otherwise PAT.
 • Tarot v3 REST:
   https://ai-platform.services.atlassian.com/api/v3/components{,/{id}/permiss
   ions, .../artifacts, .../versions} — Slauth + atlas ml registry CLI.
 • Tecton: SDK uses Databricks PAT exchanged via
   /api/2.0/token-management/on-behalf-of/tokens (workspace
   atlassian-tecton-prod); online needs TECTON_API_KEY.
 • Databricks Jobs 2.1 (/jobs/{create, run-now, runs/submit, runs/get, 
   runs/get-output, runs/cancel}) + SQL Statements API /api/2.0/sql/statements
   + Unity Catalog /api/2.1/unity-catalog/{catalogs,schemas,tables}.
 • Lineage tables: core_ml_data.{coreml_upstream_dependencies, 
   coreml_feature_quality_profiles, coreml_model_registry_tracker}.

3. Tooling convention to mirror. All three new tools should follow the
action‑keyed multi‑tool MCP pattern used by socrates/compass/bitbucket (one
function, action enum, JSON‑Schema params, {error,message} envelope, quiet
flag) and the ~/.agents/skills/twg/SKILL.md skill format (front‑matter +
Overview + scripts + Prereqs + numbered Workflow + Common patterns +
References).

4. Reusable code in responsible-ai-api
(bitbucket.org/atlassian/responsible-ai-api, master): top‑level .agents/ +
model_onboarding/ directories — Tarot v3 onboarding already implemented; new
tools should be siblings under responsible_ai_api/agents/tools/{mlreg,fs,dbx}
sharing clients/{databricks,mlflow,tarot,tecton,mlfs,socrates}.py.

5. Capability matrices + draft API contracts delivered for three tools: mlreg
(15 commands), fs (10 commands), dbx (14 commands) — each with inputs,
outputs, backing API, auth, and autonomy tier (🟢/🟡/🔴).

6. Bit‑exact MLflow metric replay (KPI 8.1) designed as a 4‑step pipeline:
capture (snapshot run + lockfiles + dataset version + replay_fingerprint SHA),
run (pinned‑cluster Jobs 2.1 submission with deterministic env vars), verify
(per‑(metric,step) comparison classified bit‑exact / ε‑exact / drift),
idempotent on replay_fingerprint.

7. Connector/region/tenant feature‑store audit designed as a templated SQL on
core_ml_data.<fv_offline> (CTE → COUNT/NULL/MAX/AVG aggregation) sliced by
(connector, region, tenant_id) producing coverage, sparsity, staleness_s,
avg_latency_s, written back to core_ml_data.coreml_feature_quality_profiles
for ML Lens consumption.

8. Gaps deliberately delegated to other subtasks: drift detection (ML Lens —
Subtask 1.2), eval triggering (Subtask 2), serving deploy (Subtask 2), CI/CD
(existing bitbucket MCP), scheduling (existing Airflow / atlas ml workflow).

9. AI‑specific patterns documented: autonomy tiers, deterministic idempotency
keys, retry/error classification, dry‑run, audit logging, and 🔴‑tier
confirmation gating envelopes.

10. Open questions (Appendix B): MLFS REST stability, exact Slauth namespaces
for Tarot writes, GPU determinism feasibility for bit‑exact replay, Tecton SDK
pinning during the MLFS migration.

