## 6. Cost & Capacity Stewardship Artifacts

### 6.1 TEAMServe GPU Capacity Management

**Source**: [TEAMServe GPU Capacity Management](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202061551fe70fbc403cbc67930b9b879754/pages/5425146514/TEAMServe+GPU+Capacity+Management)

**Four-pillar framework**:
1. **Capacity Planning**: Collect/predict needs, translate model traffic to GPU requirements
2. **Capacity Provision**: Acquire GPUs and provision to clusters
3. **Capacity Monitoring**: Report allocations, usage, model traffic health, costs (cost per call/query)
4. **Capacity Optimization**: Maximize usage, increase serving efficiency, maximize compute discounts, enable fungibility

### 6.2 SageMaker→TEAMServe Migration Heuristics

**Source**: [TEAMServe & SageMaker Cost Optimization Plan H1FY2026](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020ff70b14e5dca488b8ea018f735980b62/pages/5982146547/TEAMServe+SageMaker+Cost+Optimization+Plan+H1FY2026), [SageMaker vs TEAMServe: Model Onboarding Comparison](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AO2/pages/6858050995/SageMaker+vs+TEAMServe+Model+Onboarding+Comparison)

**Migration decision heuristics**:
- 50-60% cost reduction moving from SageMaker → TEAMServe
- Multi-model packing:3 models on shared GPUs → 12 GPUs → 4 GPUs (40% cost reduction)
- GPU → CPU migration for embeddings: $925K-$1.25M/year savings, 74-97% cost reduction
- Idle endpoint cleanup: reduced from +60k/day to ~36k/day ($8.7M/year savings)

**Classification**: **Both skill-encodable AND tool-automatable**
- *Skill-encodable*: Cost stewardship skill encodes decision heuristics (when to migrate, capacity right-sizing thresholds, reporting cadence)
- *Tool-automatable*: serving-infra tool queries GPU utilization, cost dashboards, idle endpoint detection

