## 7. Symphony3-Tier Autonomy Framework

**Source**: [Atlassian Symphony: AI Employee Orchestration Platform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6933824809/Atlassian+Symphony+AI+Employee+Orchestration+Platform)

**3-Tier Trust Framework**:
| Tier | Signal | Meaning |
|------|--------|---------|
| 1 — Autonomous | 🟢 | Agent acts without human approval. Known pattern, bounded blast radius |
| 2 — Confirm | 🟡 | Agent proposes with reasoning. Human approves single-click |
| 3 — Escalate | 🔴 | Hard policy boundary. Pages human with full context and reasoning trace |

**Orchestration loop**: Watch → Bootstrap → Execute → Supervise → Close → Learn

**Classification**: **Skill-encodable** (every skill's SKILL.md must tag each operation with the correct tier and require manifest discipline fields)

---

## 8. JSM Incident Management Metrics

**Source**: [Defining JSM MTTR](https://home.atlassian.com/o/2346a038-3c8c-498b-a79b-e7847859868d/s/a436116f-02ce-4520-8fbb-7301462a1674/project/ATLAS-61444)

**Metric definitions**:
- **TTD (Time to Detect)**: From first alert creation to incident creation
- **TTH (Time to Handle/Triage)**: From incident creation to first responder engagement
- **TTR (Time to Resolve)**: From incident creation to "Resolved" status
- **TTC (Time to Close)**: From resolution to root cause addressal (PIR + Change Management)

**Phase 1**: Issue creation → Resolved (Resolve Stage)
**Phase 2**: First alert → Resolved (Detect Phase)
**Phase 3**: First alert → Root cause resolved via PIR/CM (Prevent Phase)

**Classification**: **Tool-automatable** (metrics computed from Jira timestamps via atlassian MCP tool)

