## 1. Primary Source Document: "Digital MLE: AI Employee Vision"

**Source**: [Digital MLE: AI Employee Vision](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/7051610727/Digital+MLE+AI+Employee+Vision)

This page serves as the **de facto "role-doc §4"** for the Digital MLE AI Employee. It defines five core responsibilities with explicit autonomy tiers (🟢/🟡/🔴) and maps the full ML lifecycle into operational patterns. The page is authored by Ke Wang and is part of the AI Employee Strategy initiative.

###1.1 Core Responsibility Areas (from the Vision doc)

| **Responsibility** | **What the digital MLE owns** | **Autonomy Level** |
|---|---|---|
| Training Data Management | Data freshness monitoring, tenant list refresh, feature coverage reporting, training/serving skew detection | 🟢 Monitoring/refresh; 🟡 New sources; 🔴 Cross-team agreements |
| Model Training & Versioning | Scheduled retraining, artifact versioning, training run summaries, multi-version offline comparison, regression detection | 🟢 Scheduled runs; 🟡 Architecture changes; 🔴 Model design |
| Offline Evaluation | SxS eval suite execution, MRR/NDCG/precision reporting, win/loss extraction, regression gate | 🟢 Eval execution; 🟡 Regression interpretation; 🔴 Go/no-go decision |
| Online Experiment Monitoring | Statsig scorecard polling, metric summary, significance assessment, launch doc population | 🟢 Monitoring/docs; 🟡 Interpretation; 🔴 Launch/rollback |
| Production Health & Ramp | Serving latency/throughput monitoring, ramp schedule tracking, latency regression alerting | 🟢 Monitoring/alerting; 🟡 Ramp progression; 🔴 Incident response |

### 1.2 mini-mle Architecture (Implementation Foundation)

The implementation foundation is **mini-mle**, which has three components:
- **Skills**: Packaged prompts with ML + MLSE context (two layers: MLSE skills for setup/onboarding, MLE skills for experiments/evaluation)
- **Harnesses**: Connectors to ML runtime (ML Fabric interactive, ML Studio) — automate job submission, build monitoring, debugging loops via Bitbucket, Jira, ML Studio CLI
- **Agent Wiki**: Progressive disclosure knowledge base for navigating large codebases

