## 5. Proactive Monitoring Workflow Pattern

### What it is
A repeatable, scheduled audit workflow that runs proactively (not reactively) to detect data quality issues before they impact model performance.

### How it works (derived from multiple Atlassian internal implementations)

#### Two-Stage Pipeline Pattern (from Feature DQ Pipeline)
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Stage 1: PROFILING (Metrics Collection) │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ For each monitored dataset/feature:     │
│  • Zero-value % per column              │
│  • Data freshness (max timestamp)│
│  • Day-over-day volume change           │
│  • Null rate per column                 │
│  • Distribution summary stats│
│  • Schema snapshot comparison           │
│ Output → metrics_table                  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
              ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Stage 2: EVALUATION (Threshold Check)   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ For each metric vs per-feature config:  │
│  • Apply thresholds                     │
│  • Derive SUCCESS / FAILURE status      │
│  • Trend comparison (DoD/WoW)           │
│ Output → dq_fact_table (with status)    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
              ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Stage 3: ALERT & REPORT                 │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  • Fatal failures → block pipeline      │
│  • Non-fatal → log for review│
│  • Generate dashboard visualizations    │
│  • Send Slack/JSM notifications         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### DQ Monitor Sub-Agent Pattern (from Proactive Intelligence Pipeline)
```
dq_monitor.py runs FIRST every session:
├── Freshness Monitor
│   └── Check row_updated_timestamp against SLA (e.g., 26h)
├── Schema Drift Detector
│   └── Compare current schema vs last known-good snapshot
│└── ⚠️ Snapshot NEVER auto-updated — always manual human action
└── Distribution Anomaly Detector
    └── Z-score, null spike, cardinality drop on critical columns└── Only runs on tables with confirmed timestamp column
```

#### Alert Routing Protocol
| Severity | Condition | Action |
|----------|-----------|--------|
| **P1(Fatal/Blocking)** | Schema change; > 50% null spike; volume drop > 80% | Block pipeline; immediate alert; DE triage required |
| **P2 (Warning)** | Distribution drift PSI > 0.25; coverage drop > 20% | Alert to team channel; flag for review |
| **P3 (Informational)** | Minor drift (0.1 < PSI < 0.25); gradual null increase | Log to dashboard; include in weekly digest |

### How it applies to the skill

#### Proactive Audit Workflow (9-Step Process)
1. **🟢 Discover datasets** — Query ML registry / feature store for monitored tables
2. **🟢 Load reference baselines** — Fetch stored reference distributions and historical metrics
3. **🟢 Profile current data** — Compute statistics, completeness, schema for each table
4. **🟢 Detect drift** — Run PSI/KS/Chi-squared against reference distributions
5. **🟢 Check freshness** — Verify data recency against SLAs
6. **🟢 Evaluate expectations** — Compare metrics against configured thresholds
7. **🟡 Classify findings** — Categorize into P1/P2/P3 severity (may need human override)
8. **🟡 Generate report** — Create structured audit report with findings, trends, recommendations
9. **🔴 Remediation decisions** — Schema snapshot updates, threshold adjustments, pipeline blocks require human approval

