## 10. Scheduling & Trigger Patterns

### What it is
When and how the proactive audit should be triggered.

### How it works

| Trigger Type | Frequency | Use Case |
|-------------|-----------|----------|
| **Scheduled (Cron)** | Daily | Routine monitoring of all registered datasets |
| **Pre-training gate** | Before every training run | Ensure data quality before model training begins |
| **Post-ingestion** | After pipeline completion | Validate new data before it's consumed |
| **Event-driven (drift alert)** | On metric threshold breach | Deep-dive audit when initial alert fires |
| **On-demand** | Manual trigger | Ad-hoc investigation |

### Integration Points
- **ML Lens Cronman**: Daily scheduled drift computation every ~5 min or daily
- **ML Studio Orchestrator**: Consume drift events from StreamHub → trigger retraining
- **dbt pipeline**: DQ checks run as part of `dbt test` phase, blocking promotion on failure

