## 2. Distribution Shift / Drift Detection Standards

### What it is
Statistical methods to detect when the distribution of features or labels has changed between a reference period and the current period, which is a leading indicator of model performance degradation.

### How it works

#### Statistical Tests by Feature Type

| Feature Type | Statistical Test | Metric | Threshold Conventions |
|-------------|-----------------|--------|----------------------|
| **Continuous** | Population Stability Index (PSI) | Divergence between binned distributions | PSI < 0.1 = no drift; 0.1–0.25 = moderate; > 0.25 = significant |
| **Continuous** | Kolmogorov-Smirnov (KS) Test | Max CDF difference, p-value | p-value < 0.05 = significant drift |
| **Continuous** | Wasserstein Distance | Earth-mover distance | Threshold = 0.1 (Evidently default); magnitude-aware |
| **Categorical** | Chi-squared Test | Whether proportions changed | p-value < 0.05 = significant |
| **Categorical** | Jensen-Shannon Divergence (JSD) | Symmetric distribution divergence | 0 = identical, 1 = maximally different; threshold ~0.1 |
| **Categorical** | PSI (adapted) | Bin-frequency divergence | PSI >= 0.2 = drift detected (Atlassian internal threshold) |
| **Any** | KL-Divergence | Information-theoretic divergence | Asymmetric; useful for directional shift analysis |

#### Reference Window Strategies

| Window Type | Description | Use Case |
|-------------|-------------|----------|
| **Training baseline** | Distribution captured at model training time | Long-term structural drift detection |
| **Rolling N-day** (default28-30days) | Trailing period of production data | Short-term operational drift |
| **Fixed reference period** | User-specified date range | Controlled comparison (e.g., post-deployment) |
| **Same-period prior year** | Seasonal comparison | Seasonality-adjusted drift |

#### Atlassian's ML Lens Implementation
- **Drift Computation Job** runs daily via Cronman
- Computes KS Test (D-statistic, p-value) and PSI for all registered features
- Metrics emitted to `feature_observability.drift.*` namespace
- Alert evaluation is **opt-in** — feature owners register alert configs via MLFS SDK
- Default thresholds: KS p-value ≤ 0.05, KS-D ≥ 0.1, PSI threshold configurable

### How it applies to the skill
The audit skill should:
1. 🟢 **Autonomously** compute drift metrics for all monitored features using the ML DQ SDK
2. 🟢 **Autonomously** compare against reference distributions (training baseline + rolling window)
3. 🟡 **Escalate** when PSI > 0.25 or KS p-value < 0.01(severe drift) — recommend retraining
4. 🔴 **Human required** for changing reference distributions or adjusting thresholds

