Local-investigation note: worker_5 and parent worker_0 contained no
Databricks-specific reference docs (no SKILL.md, tool.json, or vendored
source), so findings are derived from Databricks' authoritative public REST
surface and from the convention implied by the listed peer toolsets (socrates,
compass, bitbucket).

Key findings

 • Auth: A single bearer model (PAT, Slauth/SP OAuth, or AAD) covers Jobs,
   Workspace, UC, and SQL Statement endpoints. Tokens and hosts are
   workspace+region bound — the AI tool must keep a per-tenant (env, 
   region)→host map.
 • Jobs 2.1 is the right surface for notebook execution. Primary ad-hoc path:
   POST /jobs/runs/submit (notebook_task with base_parameters,
   existing_cluster_id or new_cluster, optional git_source for commit pinning,
   idempotency_token) → poll GET /runs/get → GET /runs/get-output. Job/run
   listing via GET /jobs/list and GET /runs/list (hard page size 25, must
   paginate). Repair/cancel/export endpoints documented.
   notebook_output.result truncates at 5 MB; runs/submit history GC'd at 60
   days.
 • Workspace 2.0 provides pre-flight (get-status, list, export) to resolve
   notebook path/language/version before submission and for diffing.
 • Unity Catalog 2.1: catalogs/schemas/tables list+get,
   lineage-tracking/table-lineage and column-lineage (core for reproducibility
   audit), connections/external-locations/storage-credentials for the
   connector/region/tenant audit, plus grants/effective-permissions. Edge:
   lineage is event-sourced and may be empty for new tables; ABAC silently
   filters list responses.
 • SQL Statement Execution 2.0 is preferred over JDBC for AI-driven querying.
   Decision matrix: INLINE+JSON_ARRAY for small reads (≤25 MiB);
   EXTERNAL_LINKS+ARROW_STREAM for large audits (15-min pre-signed link
   expiry; chunked via get-result-chunk). Always use named parameter binding
   (never string-format SQL).
 • Workflow coverage: notebook execution, job listing, and UC table queries
   are fully covered by the API surface above. Bit-exact MLflow replay (KPI
   8.1) requires composing Jobs runs/submit (with pinned git_commit + pinned
   cluster spec + idempotency token) with the MLflow client (sibling worker);
   ε=0 for floats is unrealistic and the contract should specify ≤1 ULP
   tolerance.
 • Connector/region audit query design: join
   system.information_schema.connections ⋈ external_locations ⋈
   storage_credentials ⋈ tables filtered by feature-store catalog/schema,
   executed via the Statement Execution API with EXTERNAL_LINKS disposition.
   Fallback to per-table lineage-tracking REST if system.* tables are not
   enabled in the metastore.

Draft MCP tool contract (mirrors socrates/compass/bitbucket conventions):
single databricks toolset with snake_case actions grouped into workspace_*,
jobs_*, uc_*, sql_*, returning a uniform {ok, host, workspace_id, request_id,
elapsed_ms, data, error} envelope. Read-only actions are fully autonomous;
jobs_run_now/submit_notebook_run autonomous only against allow-listed notebook
paths or non-prod clusters; DDL/DML SQL and jobs_create/reset/update/delete
require user confirmation with diff preview. Retry on 429/5xx with exponential
backoff + Retry-After; never retry 4xx auth/permission/validation errors.
Adaptive polling cadence (2s→5s→10s) for runs/wait and sql_get_status.

Reuse vs. build: standardise on databricks-sdk-py>=0.30 as the HTTP/auth
client (handles PAT/OAuth/AAD/retries and exposes a 1:1 mapping to every
action in the proposed contract). Build only the thin action adapter,
lineage-graph normaliser, and Slauth credentials_provider plug-in.


Open items for synthesis: per-workspace vs. multi-workspace process model;
idempotency-token strategy for replay; metastore system-table availability;
numeric tolerance for KPI 8.1; convention for >5 MB notebook outputs (UC
volume + URI return).
