Process shape: Two-phase gating — pre_experiment (blocks A/B launch) and
pre_production (blocks GA), with intake ≥2 weeks lead time and approval by a
Review Committee (Ashley Chin, Shuguang Zhang, Qinlong Luo).

Four focal gates extracted:

 1 Privacy Review — "Privacy and security review" + optional
   "Fairness/compliance review". MUST at pre-production (template); proposal
   lists optional at pre-experiment (inconsistency flagged). Owner: PM.
   Cross-references OneTrust codes OT-01/OT-05/CM-04 used by sibling Legal
   Launch Checklist (ProdLegal space).
 2 Rollback Plan — "Model roll-back plan". MUST at pre-production, OPT
   pre-experiment. Owner: MLE. Category: Model Deployment.
 3 Drift Monitor — "Data/feature drifting monitor" + companion "Model
   inference metrics monitor" (model + business metrics) + "Infra health
   monitor". All MUST at pre-production. Owner: MLE.
 4 Alerting — "Opsgenie/alerts to Slack" on job failure. The only monitoring
   item that is MUST at BOTH phases. Owner: MLE.

Full item × phase × severity matrix (19 pre-exp items, 10 pre-prod items) is
in §2 of the report, plus a recommended YAML/JSON gate schema in §4 and a
GateEvaluator Python sketch.

Coverage: Template covers two-phase gating, severities, owners, named tooling
(Statsig, GASV3, Opsgenie, Databricks/MLflow, GRS/GUPS).

Gaps the (1C) eval-framework tool must add (greenfield — no local tool.json
for ML launch review exists; ~/.agents/skills/ contains only twg): multi-seed
mean±std offline eval, per-slice fairness thresholds (currently optional),
calibration & CIs, quantitative SLA/latency budgets, automated typed-artifact
verification (MLflow run, registry version, Opsgenie team, Statsig
experiment), drift thresholds (PSI/KS), model card, released-traffic online
eval guardrails, reconciliation with Legal Launch Checklist three-stage gates
(Privacy/Beta/GA).

Integration pattern: Confluence MCP for checklist read/write;
MLflow/Databricks for offline-eval evidence; Statsig + GASV3 for experiment
setup proofs; Opsgenie for alert routing; Bitbucket/Compass for "code-reviewed
in repo" sub-requirements; Jira for blocker tickets; OneTrust for privacy
codes; Slack for decision broadcast. Read & dry-run gate evaluation can be
autonomous; updating committee status, transitioning Jira approvals, and
external-team Slack posts require human confirmation. Evidence-link
dereference failures should downgrade to "evidence-missing" rather than
auto-pass; rate-limited Databricks calls need exponential backoff.


Proposed tool surface (§7): mlreview.create_checklist, list_items,
attach_evidence, evaluate_gate, submit_for_review, record_decision,
diff_against_template.
