   (MLflow exp 112478210483360) + --save-data (Socrates zone_ai_experience)

Normalized EvalRun envelope (designed to satisfy C1–C9):

 • Identity + reproducibility envelope (git_sha, dataset_hash, env_lock,
   cli_invocation, seed_list)
 • seeds[] + per_seed[*].metrics + aggregate{mean, std, ci_low, ci_high, 
   ci_method=bootstrap_bca} → C1 + C5
 • k_fold.scheme ∈ {stratified, time-series, group-aware} → C2
 • per_slice[dim][value][metric] → C3
 • calibration{ece, mce, brier, reliability_diagram_uri, bins=15} → C4
 • fairness[protected_dim]{demographic_parity, equalized_odds_difference, 
   selection_rate} (via fairlearn.MetricFrame) → C6
 • failure_taxonomy{data_quality, model_limitation, feature_gap, label_noise,
   distribution_shift} → C7
 • leakage_audit.group_id_straddles_splits → C8
 • negative_result{why_not_uri, lessons_uri, reusable_artifacts} (required if
   outcome ≠ shipped) → C9
 • Optional significance{paired bootstrap/Wilcoxon/McNemar + BH-FDR(slices) /
   Holm(models)}

Rigor defaults: seeds = 3 ideation / 5 ship / 10 headline; bootstrap B =
1000–10 000 BCa; ECE 15 adaptive bins; 5-fold StratifiedGroupKFold (or
TimeSeriesSplit + gap); κ ≥ 0.6 rater gate; declared pre-run threshold.yaml.
Refusal policy: ANY C1–C9 fail → emit blocked.

Major gaps the new tool must close (not present in native CLI/SDK): multi-seed
orchestration, k-fold splitter, slice auto-iteration, calibration helpers,
bootstrap CIs, paired-significance + multiple-testing correction,
failure-taxonomy classifier, reproducibility envelope, leakage audit, and
unified rovo+AIX result schema.

