   The ai-employee-mle skill has zero feature-store coverage. The MCP tool
   must be net-new but built on a well-documented internal pattern.
 2 Tecton SDK (Python) read surface to wrap:
   FeatureView.get_features_for_events() (preferred — supports
   FEATURE_TIMESTAMP/BATCH_WINDOW modes), get_online_features(),
   get_historical_features(), materialization_status(),
   materialization_history(), tecton.list_feature_views(). Workspace = region
   dimension; source name = connector dimension; auth via TECTON_API_KEY
   minted from Databricks PAT via
   /api/2.0/token-management/on-behalf-of/tokens.
 3 MLFS has three SDK surfaces: Python (atlassian-mlp-featurestore-sdk with
   core.dsl, core.sources, core.services, client.offline, client.online,
   migration extras), Java (com.atlassian.mlp.featurestore:java-client-sdk —
   production read), and HTTP/OpenAPI (POST /feature-service/{name}/serve, GET
   /feature-view/{name}/materialization-status). DSL classes include
   FeatureService, MlfsProviderConfig, TectonProviderConfig, ShadowConfig,
   FeatureViewRef, BatchMaterializationConfig, OnlineMaterializationConfig,
   Aggregate/AggregationFunction, TimeWindow.
 4 Online/offline consistency check pattern is production-validated at
   30.9M-row scale (page 7027917305). Canonical metric set: mutually-exclusive
   null classification
   (both_null/tecton_only_null/mlfs_only_null/both_non_null), exact-match with
   rtol=1e-9 atol=1e-12, Jaccard for arrays, paired-array comparison,
   p50/p90/p95/p99 diffs with direction. Three modes proposed: offline batch
   parity, online shadow via ShadowConfig DSL, and synchronous online spot
   check.
 5 Coverage / freshness / sparsity audit query design sliced by connector × 
   region × tenant_bucket. Coverage = non-null-rate via Databricks SQL on the
   MLFS offline Delta; freshness = the conservative of
   materialization_status() and MAX(_effective_at) data-plane signal vs 2× 
   batch_schedule SLA; sparsity = per-tenant null-rate distribution bucketed
   into always-null / sometimes-null / never-null with top-N drill-down
   (mirrors the "16.5K always-null tenants" prod finding). All audits use the
   existing databricks-sdk WorkspaceClient pattern in
   tools/virtual-office/workspace/MLE/05_pull_plato_hello_sample.py — biggest
   reuse opportunity.
 6 Capability matrix provided with 11 ops × inputs × outputs × auth × backing
   API; tool emits day-one preset that runs coverage + freshness + sparsity +
   consistency in one pass and writes to
   core_ml_data.coreml_feature_quality_profiles (consumed by ML Lens).
 7 Gotchas to bake in: MLP-10065 BATCH_WINDOW bug (default to
   FEATURE_TIMESTAMP), MLFS TimeWindow offset not implemented (warn-not-fail),
   MLFS backfills 91.7% higher than Tecton on aggregates (surface
   direction-of-drift), tecton_passthrough hybrid serving requires per-FV
   provider decomposition before comparison, Tecton shutdown 2026-11-30.
 8 Confluence artifacts saved for future implementation reference: BFV
   migration toolkit, MLFS adoption guide, extended serving options, offline
   comparison report (all in artifacts/).
