SPIKE: ML Evaluation Framework (page 6098222361) — Compares rovo-eval
(go/rovoeval, Kotlin centralized service, excellent ConvoAI + UI + multi-turn
user simulation, but poor ML Studio integration, Kotlin-barrier custom
metrics, no production data access, queue delays up to a day) vs AIX-eval
(Python library at bitbucket.org/atlassian/ai-experience-evaluation, ML Studio
module at modules/src/ai_experience/aixeval_run/, excellent ML Studio +
Databricks + MLflow + UGC data + prompt tuning + custom Python metrics, but no
built-in user simulation, requires ConvoAI client integration).
Recommendation: use AIX-eval for TWG apps + keep rovo-eval for ConvoAI agents.
Eight requirements enumerated: ConvoAI integration, test automation, ML Studio
integration, user simulation, prompt tuning, metrics calculations, dashboard,
Slack alerting. External tools (Arize, Braintrust) rejected due to
data-sharing/integration risk.

End-to-End ML Framework @ Atlassian (page 6708596091) — Canonical pipeline:
Data Lake → Databricks/MLflow → ML Studio → MSP/ML Registry (Tarot v3) → 
SageMaker / TEAMServe-Triton → Micros service. Key primitives identified:
groupName + versionTag (the bridge between MSP and Micros .sd.yml), MLflow run
URIs (runs:/<run_id>/model), atlassian-msp-sdk for upload/register,
inference.py (SageMaker: model_fn/input_fn/predict_fn/output_fn) vs Triton
TritonPythonModel (initialize/execute/finalize). Rollback = flip versionTag
and redeploy. Existing automation uses Bitbucket Pipelines (e.g., CTPMP-385);
ML Studio CMCD is the "CI/CD for models" target. Tarot v3 supersedes V2;
lineage requires createdBy/systemMetadata/userMetadata. AI Gateway and 3P SaaS
AI are explicitly out of scope — so tool 1A must extend beyond.

Gaps the new tools must fill:

 • 1C: multi-seed mean±std, per-slice metrics, calibration, CIs, fairness, ML
   Launch Review Checklist gate logic, Slack alerting, unified rovo+AIX
   dashboard — none first-class today.
 • 1A: AI Gateway routing, canary/shadow primitives (only versionTag-flip
   rollback exists), autoscaling tuning surface.
 • 1B: Spinnaker REST + .sd.yml editing distinct from Bitbucket Pipelines
   (must avoid duplication).

Recommended design patterns (1D): model identity = (groupName, versionTag,
mlflow_run_id); source of truth = Bitbucket (emit PRs/diffs); compose via ML
Studio modules; wrap MSP SDK + MLflow + Spinnaker calls with structured
retry/error handling; gate production writes (versionTag flips, released-tier
registrations, prod Slack alerts) behind human confirmation per existing PR +
PRGB + manual-pipeline pattern.


