   net-new. No reusable client wrappers exist in responsible-ai-api; we just
   reuse its ASAP auth pattern.
 3 Capability matrices delivered (with inputs × outputs × backing API ×
   autonomy tier):
    • mlflow_tarot — 20 actions: experiment/run CRUD, batch logging,
      run_log_model (multi-framework), Tarot v3 typed-component registration,
      lineage, stage transitions, replay_verify, experiment_kpi_8_1_report.
    • feature_store — 16 actions across Tecton + MLFS via a facade resolver:
      fv_*, get_historical_features, get_online_features, consistency_check,
      audit_freshness/coverage/sparsity/full, lineage_get,
      online_offline_skew_alarm, dataset_register.
    • databricks_uc — 21 actions: Notebooks Workspace API, Jobs API 2.1
      (runs/submit, runs/get, etc.), Unity Catalog REST
      (catalogs/schemas/tables/grants/history), and SQL Statements API with
      cost + DML guardrails.
 4 Bit-exact MLflow replay (KPI 8.1) — 6-step protocol: freeze inputs
   (params/tags/dataset lineage/container digest) → reconstruct env (pinned
   container + pip digests + deterministic env vars) → pin data (Delta VERSION
   AS OF + Tecton FV commit hash + Parquet SHA256 check) → re-execute →
   bit-exact metric compare (struct.pack('>d',x) byte comparison) or tolerant
   mode → persist as Tarot "reproducibility_report" artifact. Failure
   taxonomy: env_drift / dataset_drift / nondeterministic_op / seed_gap / 
   numerical_instability / lineage_incomplete.
 5 Connector/region/tenant FS audit query — single composed UC SQL using
   GROUPING SETS for one-pass coverage + sparsity stratified by connector × 
   region × tenant × segment, with previous-window baseline diff (delta_pp),
   aggregate-FV TTL-aware STALE detection, and upstream-table fallback when
   dimension columns are absent.
 6 Composition patterns documented for: (A) replay verification, (B) proactive
   data-quality audit, (C) drift-triggered retraining end-to-end SOP-1, (D)
   online/offline consistency. Shared common/auth.py + Envelope + retry +
