**Description**: CREATE the serving + CI/CD + eval tools, PLUS the AI-MLE operating-procedure skill bundle. NEW TOOLS: (1) Serving-infra tool (TEAMServe / SageMaker / AI Gateway / Launchpad) — list endpoints, deploy/rollback canary + shadow, configure AI Gateway routing patterns (OpenAI / Anthropic / Bedrock / Gemini / internal), query endpoint health, tune autoscaling, exercise the TEAMServe gRPC endpoint pattern (`grpc-teamserve-{region}.{env}.services.kitt-inf.net:443`) — drives Responsibility 6, SOP-1 steps 6–7, SOP-3 step 5, and cost-stewardship work. (2) ML CI/CD tool (Spinnaker + Micros service descriptors) — list/start/inspect Spinnaker pipelines for ML deploys and read/edit Micros service descriptors for owned services. DO NOT duplicate Bitbucket Pipelines (already covered by the bitbucket MCP). Drives Responsibility 6/7. (3) Eval-framework tool (rovo-eval + AIX-eval) — trigger offline / adhoc / released eval workflows, pull results with mean ± std multi-seed, per-slice metrics, calibration, CIs, fairness, and enforce ML Launch Review Checklist gates — drives Responsibility 8, SOP-1 step 4, SOP-2 steps 5–7. NEW SKILLS (SKILL.md files leveraging Subtask 1 tools + Subtask 2 tools + existing MCPs): (a) SOP-1 Drift-Triggered Retraining skill — encodes the 9-step procedure with 🟢/🟡/🔴 autonomy tiers. (b) SOP-2 New Experiment Cycle skill — hypothesis → literature synthesis → 5–10 parallel architectures → mandatory ablation → exhaustive error analysis → decision. (c) SOP-3 Production Incident Response skill — circuit breaker activation, 30-min Slack cadence, auto-drafted PIR within 5 BD (Confluence + Jira), TTD/TTH/TTR/TTC tracking. (d) ML Launch Review Checklist gate skill — automated gates (privacy review, rollback plan, drift monitor, alerting). (e) Proactive data-quality audit skill — feature coverage / sparsity audit before training. (f) Reporting & templates skill — Model Card, Experiment Report (including negative results), Deployment Manifest, Architecture Comparison Report, Weekly Experiment Digest, authored as byproducts to Confluence. (g) Symphony 3-tier autonomy + manifest discipline skill — every autonomous change emits the non-negotiable manifest (intent, non-goals, impacted services/files, declared invariants, risk classification, test plan, rollback plan, post-deploy monitoring plan) and applies calibrated uncertainty. (h) Cost & capacity stewardship skill — FinOps dashboards + ML Artifact Cost Monitoring + SageMaker → TEAMServe migration recommendation pattern. (i) Literature & prior-experiment synthesis skill — SOP-2 step 2 synthesis pattern. WHY existing tools insufficient: Spinnaker, Micros descriptors, TEAMServe, SageMaker, AI Gateway, Launchpad, rovo-eval, AIX-eval have no MCP coverage; and only the `twg` skill exists locally — none of the SOP/reporting/autonomy skills above exist. Each new skill is needed because it encodes a workflow not currently captured anywhere. RESEARCH REQUIREMENT: investigate responsible-ai-api codebase + ML Studio / TEAMServe / Spinnaker docs + SPIKE: ML Evaluation Framework + ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook + End-to-End ML Framework @ Atlassian; evaluate each runbook/eval framework/query pattern in role-doc §4 as a direct skill or tool candidate.

**Todos**:
- Research and build the serving-infra tool covering TEAMServe, SageMaker, AI Gateway routing, and Launchpad, including canary/shadow rollout primitives and autoscaling tuning.
- Research and build the Spinnaker + Micros service-descriptor tool for ML deploy orchestration (explicitly avoid duplicating Bitbucket Pipelines functionality already in the bitbucket MCP).
- Research and build the rovo-eval + AIX-eval tool that runs the 6-stage eval protocol with multi-seed mean ± std, slice metrics, calibration, CIs, and fairness, and gates against the ML Launch Review Checklist.
- Author SKILL.md for SOP-1 Drift-Triggered Retraining, SOP-2 New Experiment Cycle, and SOP-3 Production Incident Response — each encoding the autonomy tiers, escalation rules, and tool sequences.
- Author SKILL.md for the ML Launch Review Checklist gate, proactive data-quality audit, reporting & templates (Model Card / Experiment Report / Deployment Manifest / Architecture Comparison / Weekly Digest), Symphony 3-tier autonomy + manifest discipline, cost & capacity stewardship, and literature/prior-experiment synthesis.
- Wire each skill to the concrete tools it invokes (Subtask 1 tools + the three tools in this subtask + existing MCPs: atlassian, bitbucket, slack, switcheroo, compass, twg, etc.) and add references to the canonical role-doc sources.
