─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Key findings the SignalFx-IaC and ML-Lens tools must consume verbatim:

 1 Canonical SLO knob set (10 fields) — slidingWindowType (TIME_BASED
   default), slidingWindowSize (60s), minimumNumberOfCalls (20),
   failureRateThreshold (20%), waitDurationInOpenState (30s base),
   permittedNumberOfCallsInHalfOpenState (20),
   automaticTransitionFromOpenToHalfOpenEnabled (true),
   exponentialBackoffMultiplier (2.0), maxWaitDurationInOpenState (60s),
   recordFailurePredicate (5xx-only via ServerErrorOnlyPredicate). Appendix
   YAML is the literal reference block — IaC tools must round-trip every field
   1-to-1.
 2 Threshold bands (from Firebolt design doc, with statistical justification
   of the ≥5% floor: mean + 3σ ≈ 1.9%): Aggressive (<5%), Balanced (10–15%,
   recommended), Conservative (15–20%, current prod), Severe-only (<50%). Trip
   math: required_failures = ceil(threshold% * effectiveWindowCalls).
 3 3-state lifecycle Closed → Open → Half-Open ↔ Closed, with automatic
   half-open transition. Maps to three detector severities: critical (open
   transition), major (stuck-open > N seconds), warning (flapping).
 4 Failure-predicate contract: 5xx-only. ML-Lens drift alerts must emit
   synthetic 503s through the ML-Engine façade to participate in the CB
   lifecycle — they cannot drive CB directly with 4xx or app-level signals.
 5 Alert payload contract (3 mandatory inline cards): Switcheroo gate
   aiops_circuit_breaker_enabled (UUID 14ae760c-ba0f-4f8f-a62d-1ecd169737f1),
   Splunk saved search "Circuit Breaker State : Open, Call not permitted", and
   design-doc backlink. SignalFx IaC must attach all three as first-class
   detector fields (runbook, feature_gate, design_doc).
 6 Tuning governance: Playbook 3 mandates Tech Lead + SRE + PM approvers,
   5–10% canary, two windows of stability — therefore any threshold-modifying
   tool operation requires human confirmation (autonomous lint/plan only).

Gaps the runbook does NOT cover (must be defined elsewhere): per-endpoint
registry, notification routing, multi-tenant fan-out, SLO/error-budget math,
drift-specific thresholds (KS/KL/cosine ≥ 0.60 floor — owned by ML-Lens
facet), composite detectors, audit log.


Deliverable produced in facet.md: capability matrix, workflow coverage matrix,
autonomy matrix (read/lint/plan = autonomous; threshold change / gate flip /
ack = human-only), full integration pattern showing how ML-Lens drift events
compose with the CB lifecycle via synthetic 5xx, and a canonical
endpoints.yaml per-endpoint SLO schema that is a 1-to-1 rename of the
runbook's configuration table with optional drift_link: block for ML-Lens
integration (including the cosine ≥ 0.60 NLP-embedding floor seam).
