                                 Key findings

ML Lens (well-documented in Confluence)

 • Architecture & SDK reference: "ML Lens: How it works" (KYC space,
   6973026460) — components (Python SDK atlassian_ml_lens_sdk + Kotlin backend
   atlassian/ml-lens), publish path (StarRocks ai_events_v via Observo), ~80s
   ingestion latency, exclusion-tag pitfalls (model_id, tenant_id, product,
   region are promoted columns and silently break tag_filters).
 • REST surface:
   https://ml-lens.sgw.prod.atl-paas.net/api/v1/alerts/{metricKey}?namespace=.
   .. via atlas slauth curl -a ml-lens -e prod -g micros-sv--ml-lens-dl-admins
   (admin group required or 403).
 • Drift design ([Design] ML Lens Platform Data Drift Detection,
   MLP/6738511349) covers only KS test + PSI + summary stats — no cosine, no 
   KL. Namespace feature_observability.drift.<metric_type>.<feature_name>;
   daily cadence default.
 • Alert config schema captured: builder DSL (AlertConfig, AlertMetricConfig,
   AlertCondition, Recipient); baselines are key-level (not tag-level);
   wildcard * only matches non-dot segments; recommended placement-encoding
   via ~ separator in metric_key.

SignalFx detectors-as-code (well-documented)

 • Three canonical Confluence pages: SignalFX - Alerting & Detectors
   (MOCA/939585357), How to codify SignalFX detectors in AX
   (AtlasPrime/786445873), HOW TO: Applying SignalFX Detectors with Terraform
   (CA3/908841335).
 • Stack: Terraform provider splunk-terraform/signalfx → signalfx_detector
   resource → SignalFlow program_text → SFM/Sauron auto-apply.
 • Severity → page: Critical/Major page on-call; Minor/Warning/Info don't.
   Required GroupBy: environment, environment_type for OpsGenie routing.
   Aperiodic data: use extrapolation='zero' +
   aperiodic.above_or_below_detector.

Gaps / first-class encoding plan

 • Cosine ≥ 0.60 NLP floor is not native to ML Lens — new tool must compute
   (centroid-cosine default), publish to new namespace
   feature_observability.drift.cosine.<feature>, auto-register
   AlertCondition(operator="<", value=0.60), and optionally mirror as SignalFx
   Critical detector for OpsGenie paging.
 • Per-endpoint SLO schema drafted as typed EndpointSLO dataclass
   (availability, latency p99/p95, error_rate, drift floors, NDCG floor,
   multi-window burn-rate windows) → synthesised into signalfx_detector
   Terraform with endpoint_id filter.
 • "ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook" not discoverable via CQL on
   hello.atlassian.net. Recommend grepping responsible-ai-api and ML-Engine
   service repo directly (likely RUNBOOK.md).
 • Observo Alerting V2 migration in progress — multiple migration pages exist;
   consider forward-compatible dual-emit.


Workflow coverage matrix, API contracts (publish, alert CRUD, 
query_drift/data-quality/model-perf/system-health, check_cosine_floor, 
EndpointSLO synth), integration patterns (drift→detect→alert→page; 
cross-platform mirror; SOP-1/SOP-3 composition), and 5 open questions for 
human confirmation are detailed in the full facet.md report.
