Key findings:

 1 API surface — ML Lens exposes 3 logical groups:
    • Metrics Ingestion: POST /api/v1/metrics (OpenAPI 3.0.3 spec; type-pinned
      by metric_key; emit via REST or atlassian_ml_lens_sdk Python SDK with
      send_metrics(run_id, [MetricsPayload]))
    • Metrics Query: GET /api/v1/metrics/{key}?metric_namespace=... (returns
      full timeseries; StarRocks-backed
      production.ai_ml_lens_data.ai_events_v2 as SQL escape hatch)
    • Alerts: POST /api/v1/alerts/register (full payload schema documented:
      alert_key, alert_namespace, alert_configs with reference_period
      absolute/relative, alert_conditions single/group/complex with measures
      std/expected_value/no_data/mean, recipients for Slack/JSM Ops with P1–P5
      priorities/StreamHub); list/diff implied via register_alerts.py; delete
      via atlas ml alerts delete CLI
 2 Drift stats are precomputed client-side —
   atlassian_ml_dq_sdk.metrics.distribution provides KolmogorovSmirnov,
   KLDivergence, PopulationStabilityIndex, FeatureDrift (PySpark). Cosine is 
   NOT in SDK — must be computed externally (NLP embedding service) and
   emitted as scalar.
 3 Dashboard taxonomy (4 pillars) from HLA: Data / Training / Feature /
   Serving Observability — queried by namespace convention, no separate REST.
 4 Alerts-as-code reference pattern (Tenant 360 HOWTO) — YAML config +
   register_alerts.py --dry-run + post-merge apply, two-stage Slack-soak → JSM
   Ops graduation, 4-retry backoff (2/5/10s) for transient 401s. This is the
   canonical pattern the new MCP tool should mirror.
 5 Cosine ≥ 0.60 floor encoding plan — first-class
   alert_register_cosine_floor(floor=0.60) helper that internally constructs
   {measure: expected_value, operator: <, value: 0.60} with a relative
   reference period.
 6 API contract draft delivered for 9-action ml_lens_queries MCP tool
   (metric_emit, metric_query, alert_register/list/delete, alerts_sync,
   drift_compute, drift_query, dashboard_query) with autonomy classification
   (read-only autonomous; soak-stage Slack-only autonomous; JSM Ops graduation
   + delete require human confirmation).
 7 Gaps to be filled by sibling tools: per-endpoint SLO encoding → SignalFx
   (worker_7); CB state machine → CB runbook (worker_8). ML Lens is the
   metric+alert spine that feeds both.


