─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Full report written to outputs/facet.md. Key findings:


 1 Three statistics, three different semantics — must NOT be collapsed into a
   single "drift score" detector:
    • KS test: D-statistic in [0,1], non-parametric CDF gap; dangerously
      over-sensitive at large N (Evidently recommends N<1000). IaC should
      expose d_threshold, not p-value.
    • KL divergence: [0,∞), unbounded, blows up on unseen categories. Use JSD
      (bounded [0,1], symmetric) as default; encode PSI/JSD bands (<0.1
      stable, 0.1–0.2 warn, >0.2 page) as a named enum.
    • Cosine similarity: [-1,1], fires when metric DROPS —
      direction-of-badness must be schema-encoded.
 2 Cosine ≥ 0.60 floor — three independent anchors converge:
    • Geometric: cosine 0.60 = mid-point of unit-hypersphere distance for
      L2-normalised embeddings.
    • MRPC paraphrase benchmark (MDPI 2025): optimal MPNet threshold = 0.671;
      performance peaks in 0.6–0.8 band across BERT/RoBERTa/MPNet → 0.60 is
      the safe lower edge.
    • Sentence-Transformers canonical example: "I'm happy" vs "I'm full of
      happiness" = 0.6003 → 0.60 is the empirical floor of semantic
      equivalence.
    • AWS SageMaker pathology example fires at 0.378 → 0.60 is the
      "early-warning" zone, not "obvious failure".
 3 Why a hard floor (not a percentile): cold-start safe, tamper-evident vs
   slow re-baselining, audit-friendly (justification reviewable by Legal).
   Should be OR-combined with a percentile detector.
 4 First-class IaC encoding plan (Terraform/Pulumi):
    • Dedicated cosine_floor { threshold, window, aggregation, baseline_ref, 
      severity, justification } block — NOT a generic threshold.
    • Required direction field per drift sub-block (eliminates "forgot to
      invert comparator" outages).
    • Required justification string flows into SignalFx detector description +
      governance docs.
    • Schema lint rejects > 0.95 (typo) and < 0.30 (won't fire).
    • Per-endpoint SLO YAML unifies ML Lens + SignalFx + Circuit Breaker
      Runbook via single drift.cosine_floor field.
    • Disallow pca_dim when metric=cosine (cosine breaks under PCA per
      Evidently).
 5 Capability matrix provided in §3 mapping signal-type → statistic → range →
   direction → IaC field → default detector.
 6 Out of scope / open questions: prompt-injection drift above 0.60 (needs
   ZEDD-style paired-prompt detector); concept drift (needs model-based
   ROC-AUC); reconciliation with existing Circuit Breaker Runbook threshold
   and role-doc §4.3 ML Lens query patterns is needed from sibling research.
