## Original User Request
**Description**: CREATE the ML platform-layer tools bundle that the AI MLE needs for tracking, registry, observability, features, and notebooks. Build the following NEW tools, each exposing executable capabilities not covered by any existing MCP toolset or local skill: (1) MLflow + ML Studio + ML Registry (Tarot v3) tool — list/search runs, log/read params + metrics, register/version models, fetch lineage, verify reproducibility (bit-exact metric replay) — drives Role-Doc Responsibilities 2/3/5, SOP-1 step 2, day-one task 1, KPI 8.1 + reproducibility audit. (2) ML Lens drift + performance tool — query drift metrics (KS / KL / cosine ≥ 0.60 for NLP embeddings), pull data-quality / model-performance / system-health dashboards, configure alerts — drives Responsibility 1, SOP-1 step 1, SOP-3 step 1, drift-score KPI. (3) SignalFx detectors-as-code tool — author/update/list SignalFx detectors via IaC, encode per-endpoint SLOs — drives Responsibility 7 and day-one task 6. (4) Feature Store (Tecton + MLFS) tool — define/list features, online/offline consistency check, audit coverage + freshness + sparsity by connector / region / tenant, lineage queries — drives Responsibility 4 and SOP-2 step 4 (proactive data-quality audit). (5) Databricks notebooks + Unity Catalog tool — execute notebooks, list jobs, query Unity Catalog tables — drives Responsibility 3 training execution. WHY existing tools are insufficient: none of the available MCP toolsets (atlassian, bitbucket, slack, compass, switcheroo, socrates, teamwork_graph, etc.) target Atlassian's internal ML platform layer (MLflow on Databricks tracking URI, Tarot v3, ML Lens, SignalFx, Tecton, MLFS, Databricks, Unity Catalog). socrates covers the vNext data lake but not Unity Catalog or the rest of the ML stack. RESEARCH REQUIREMENT: discover internal SDKs, API endpoints, CLIs, runbooks, and existing automation for each platform — review responsible-ai-api codebase, MLOps@CoreML Long-Term Plan, Building ML Models in vNext with MLflow, ML Studio One-Pager, Feature Store Implementation Plan, and the canonical MLflow run construction / Feature Store lifecycle / ML Lens query patterns described in role-doc §4.3.

**Todos**:
- Research Atlassian-internal SDKs / APIs / CLIs for MLflow on Databricks tracking URI, ML Studio, and ML Registry (Tarot v3); design and implement the unified tracking+registry tool with run/param/metric/lineage/reproducibility operations.
- Research ML Lens APIs and build a tool that queries drift (KS, KL, cosine), data-quality, model-performance, and system-health dashboards and configures alerts; encode the cosine ≥ 0.60 NLP-embedding floor as a first-class check.
- Research SignalFx IaC patterns from responsible-ai-api and ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook; build a detectors-as-code tool that creates/updates/lists detectors and encodes per-endpoint SLOs.
- Research Tecton + MLFS APIs and feature-store lifecycle from role-doc §4.3; build a feature-store tool covering definition, online/offline consistency, and coverage/freshness/sparsity audit by connector/region/tenant.
- Research Databricks + Unity Catalog APIs; build a tool for notebook execution, job listing, and Unity Catalog table queries that the training SOPs will invoke.
- For each tool, document the API contract (inputs/outputs/auth) so Subtask 2's SOP skills can integrate against a stable surface.
</UserRequest>

